WEBVTT

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.690
<i>"And now they cover the Tatsuta River like a gorgeous brocade of silk."</i>

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.450
So you have the same 
specialty cards as your master?

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.700
This is all thanks to you.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.240
Ooka Momiji...

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.350
I'll have to give you my thanks once today's TV recording is over.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.850
Oh? 
You're early.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.590
You came already?

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.610
Y-You?! What happened?!

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.760
D-Don't tell me that...

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.230
<i>"...after lying dormant all winter."</i>

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:08.980
<i>"Now the spring has come 
and the flowers are blossoming."</i>

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:18.340
<i>"Now the spring has come 
and the flowers are blossoming."</i>

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.640
<i>"Because I left in a hurry on this journey, 
I failed to even bring something to offer at the shrine."</i>

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.710
<i>"Please accept the dazzling blanket of autumn leaves over Mt. Tamukeyama as an offering from my heart."</i>

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.410
Whoa.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.720
One of the karuta cards 
came flying all the way over here?

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.270
Oh, please do not 
trouble yourself with that.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.410
What? Alright.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.170
I apologize for disturbing you.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.930
She's so cute!

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.670
Come on, Dad! 
Keep it down!

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:35.930
She looks amazing!

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.130
Just like a movie star!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.800
Her kimono suits her well, too!

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.710
Wait.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.370
Why are we here, 
watching a karuta match again?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.590
Ain't that why Mikiko was sayin'...

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.500
"This's before our discussion, 
so wait in the waitin' room"?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.250
But then ya go 'n got 
lured in by that pretty lady...

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.320
And walked 
right in to the studio.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.560
Who's this "Mikiko"?

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.270
Didn't I just introduce ya?!

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.780
That girl with glasses playing 
karuta against the pretty lady!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.890
She's the prez of the karuta club 
I'm in at our very own Kaiho Academy!

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.410
By "I'm in"...

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.480
Were ya in the 
karuta club, Kazuha?

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.540
Yeah! 
Ya didn't know?

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.370
Anyway, don'tcha think ya two took a little too long in the restroom, Heiji?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.270
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.420
The doors to the 
studio were closed 'n all...

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.960
And I didn't know whether 
or not it was okay to open 'em.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.300
Excuse me.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.510
We're in the middle of rehearsal, 
so can we have you be a little quieter?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.260
Y-Yes, sir.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.980
<i>"Though I felt I would 
gladly give up my life for you..."</i>

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.080
Wow!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:31.980
Hey, Kudo.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.250
Don'cha think the old man's forgettin' he came to Osaka to have a discussion?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.780
Give him a break.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.770
After all, the kids kept pestering him, 
saying that they wanted to sightsee in Osaka...

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.950
And he brought them in place of the professor, who had something come up and couldn't come.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.200
In that case, 
what 'bout that rich girl?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.080
Oh. 
If you mean Sonoko...

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.080
She's down with a cold.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.000
But I had no idea you were part of the karuta club, Kazuha-chan!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.780
I do it 'long 
side the aikido club!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.950
The karuta club was about to disband 'cause of a lack of new members...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.240
So they asked me 
just to add my name.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.420
I participate every now and then to come to Mikiko's practices.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.290
I'm kinda like 
a zombie member!

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.020
A 'zombie member'? That's funny!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.770
You two lively ladies 
seem to be enjoying yourselves.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.400
Almost as if you're at a café.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.570
We're sorry!

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:43.380
I'm high school detective, Kudo Shinichi.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.740
While visiting an amusement park with my childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran...

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.630
I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.370
While caught up in watching the deal...

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.130
I failed to notice his 
partner sneaking up behind me.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.420
That man forced me to take poison...

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.940
And when I came to...

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.860
My body had shrunk.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.530
If those guys found out that 
Kudo Shinichi was still alive...

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:20.750
They'd come after me again, and put those around me at risk.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.170
At Professor Agasa's suggestion, 
I decided to hide my true identity.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.890
And the moment 
Ran asked for my name...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.620
I became Edogawa Conan.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.540
In order to obtain 
information on those guys...

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.460
I went to live with Ran, 
whose father is a private detective.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.060
This is Hattori Heiji, 
the High School Detective of the West.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.390
Using the powers of deduction he inherited from his father, the superintendent of the Osaka Police...

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.140
He solves countless difficult cases...

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.040
And is one of the few 
who know my true identity.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.070
Toyama Kazuha.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.730
Classmate and
childhood friend of Hattori.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:02.590
In Hattori's words, 
"she's always getting jealous".

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.860
What lies ahead for these two?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:09.570
And lastly, the future queen, 
who's shrouded in mystery.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.600
Who exactly is she?

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:14.770
Even though I've shrunk, 
my mind remains the same...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.890
That of an unbeaten great detective.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.820
There's always only one truth!

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.820
There's always only one truth!

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.190
Man...

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:31.400
We come to a TV studio, and we're stuck in the waiting room?

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.230
I wanted to see 
the real take, too...

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:34.400
That's not possible.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.820
Because they were 
even angry with Mr. Kogoro.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:37.930
I'm sorry.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.540
This is my fault, 
for getting so loud.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.000
Oh, I know!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.610
Once everyone's back, how about we go buy some souvenirs?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:44.050
What?!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:44.580
Really?!

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:45.170
Seriously?!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:45.860
Yes.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.130
If you guys are good and behave until the recording is over, that is.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.440
Of course!

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.120
Alright!

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.790
Let's all go shopping together!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.070
Speaking of which...

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.700
What happened to Conan-kun?

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.140
Oh, about Conan-kun...

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.210
He's keeping an eye 
on Dad in my place.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.720
Hey, boy.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.150
Didn't they tell you to go 
wait in the waiting room, too?

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.390
But Ran-neechan asked me to come keep an eye on how the recording is going.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.420
Jeez.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.400
All right, clear the way!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.070
Please open a path!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.160
Karuta cards coming through!

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.280
Wow! Those're the 
Satsuki Cup karuta cards!

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.140
They're really playin' up 
those karuta cards, aren't they?

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.660
What're ya sayin', Kazuha?

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.860
In the Satsuki Cup...

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.630
Those are the legendary karuta cards used in the final match of the nationals, ain't they?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.250
Oh, yeah...

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.110
Playin' a match with those cards was your dream, wasn't it, Mikiko?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.230
Not just mine.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.340
In the 20-year history of the Satsuki Cup...

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.640
There ain't no one who hasn't 
longed to hold those cards.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:40.770
Oh, how I'd like to touch those legendary cards in the finals, even just once.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:41.440
Hey...

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.560
Why are those cards 
only used in the final?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.360
They've been through many intense matches, so they're badly damaged.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.580
And so, other than when 
they're used in the final...

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:56.270
They're put in a case like that, and usually on display in an art museum.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:59.690
Even so, don'cha think those guards're 
makin' too big of a deal about them?

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.020
No, they're not!

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.670
There was a big panic after last year's Satsuki Cup, when the karuta cards disappeared.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.040
In the end, the cards 
were found right away...

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.320
But by saying security 
aught to be tightened...

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.930
It seems the reigning champ, Yajima-san, satisfied Chairman Achiwa.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.930
Satsuki Cup

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.930
~Come, Let Us Fight Through 
\h\hthe Hyakunin Isshu!!~

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.200
I see.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.520
By the way...

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.470
Who are those two, again?

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.260
Are ya an idiot, old man?!

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.660
Ain't those the people 
you're about to meet with?!

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.640
Oh, are they?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.520
Consistent as ever, old man...

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.810
The president, 
Achiwa Kensuke, is pictured here.

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:30.320
Oh?

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.890
He's a bigwig who both established and built up Achiwa Real Estate throughout his lifetime...

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:35.820
And is even called the 
Real Estate King of Naniwa.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.870
If that's him, why is a 
man like that managing karuta?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.010
It seems it's his only hobby.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.790
Apparently, he's got 
considerable skill at it, too.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.240
But it says here that Achiwa-san himself wanted to be a card reader rather than a player.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.070
Whoa! 
Who's that beautiful woman?!

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.410
That's Satsuki-san, Achiwa-san's wife.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.470
What? She's married?

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.350
The Satsuki Cup was originally created by Satsuki-san, when she was the queen...

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.870
And Achiwa-san became the 
chairman of it as her successor.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.970
Another thing that looks like 
it'll come up at the discussion...

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:07.860
Oh, doesn't this 
seem kind of interesting?

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:12.720
When Achiwa-san holds his wife Satsuki-san's important matches...

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.860
It says he's superstitious about making sure his car's washed the day before.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.440
He's saying that making his car clean is a key to her success and victory.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:24.600
So, is it okay for me to have a three-person 
discussion with this superstitious couple?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.710
No...

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:30.590
His wife, Satsuki-san, passed away due to illness three years ago.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:34.360
Today's discussion will be 
with only Chairman Achiwa.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.590
I-Is that so?

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.930
Um...

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:41.100
Who's this really strong-looking guy who's always beside Achiwa-san in the pictures?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.890
Oh, he's Kaieda Tougo-san, 
who acted as Achiwa-san's secretary.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:49.770
Word is that he's a sharp man, having been fully responsible for managing Achiwa Real Estate behind the scenes...

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.520
But he quit as the secretary, 
and as for where he is now...

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:53.400
Hey, Hattori-kun!

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.260
Stop saying such baseless things!

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.430
The chairman of the Satsuki Cup ain't got no one "behind the scenes"!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.490
Yeah, Heiji!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.890
Now, now... 
That's the rumor. The rumor.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.450
The chairman's entering the studio!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.460
It's Chairman Achiwa! 
I've gotta greet him!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.320
It's a pleasure to work 
with you today, Mr. Chairman.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.870
Yes, same to you. 
It's a pleasure to have you.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:12.340
Yes, sir.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:17.130
I hear there's a demonstration with Yajima-kun and Momiji-kun today...

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.630
Followed by the match, correct?

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.780
Yes.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:23.640
And when we're on air, we'll show the charm and appeal of karuta to the whole nation...

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.330
By featuring the Satsuki Cup's 
special karuta collection...

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.650
Of which, through Yajima-san's cooperation, we obtained last week!

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.530
Oh! So you already have the 
Satsuki Cup karuta on display?

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.200
Well then, 
I'm really counting on you.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:35.570
Yes, sir.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.510
What incredible dignity.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.510
Yeah. That's the 
"Real Estate King of Naniwa" for ya!

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:41.340
Excuse me!

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.580
Has anyone been 
able to contact Yajima-san?

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.330
It's almost time 
he's gotta be here...

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.440
But we can't get 
a hold of him at all.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.830
That's certainly strange.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.370
He said he would come in 
an hour before the actual recording.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.960
For the always-punctual 
Yajima-kun to be late...

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.220
Go tell Sekine-kun to 
come in as well, just in case.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.720
In the worst-case scenario, 
we'll have him come in as a substitute.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.950
D-Don't tell me he...

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.460
Time opened up until filming starts.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.330
Yeah, it did.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.850
So Heiji, where d'ya 
wanna go for some okonomiyaki?

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.460
Well, ain't <i>that</i> the first place ya think of when ya say okonomiyaki?

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.750
Yeah! When ya say 
okonomiyaki, it's gotta be...

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.840
I'm sorry. 
Are you okay?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.840
You're the one who 
was playin' karuta earlier...

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.040
This is destiny.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:46.390
Huh?

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.040
I thought I'd 
never see you again...

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:49.770
What?

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.440
My future husband!

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:53.350
Her future...

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.340
Husband?!

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.050
<i>WHAT...?!</i>

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.400
I'm free after filming is done.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.910
If you'd like, 
could we talk afterwards?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.910
Whoa... 
This girl's boobs are huge!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.690
W-W-Wait, what're you...?!

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:05.560
W-Well, um...

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:06.440
Momiji-san!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.630
I'm sorry, but please return to the waiting room for the time being.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.910
Oh? I had just 
gotten to the good part, too.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:15.110
Actually, 
Yajima-san is late in arriving...

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:16.290
Yajima-san?

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:20.030
Well, he <i>is</i> the one 
who planned this program...

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.300
So I'm sure there's 
a lot he's busy with.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.800
Well, I'll see ya later, Heiji-kun.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.320
Yeah, see ya.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.310
Who the hell was that broad?!

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.210
That's the pretty 
lady from before!

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:32.320
She really is beautiful!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.290
I'm sure he said "Momiji-san"...

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.610
Ain't that why I'm 
sayin' I don't know her?!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.720
But she knew 
your name was "Heiji"!

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:39.820
Ran-oneesan.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.730
So come on 'n spill, already!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.630
Let's wait outside ahead of them.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.970
Ain't ya gettin' angry over nothin'?!

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:43.800
Looks like they're having 
some kind of argument, and all.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:43.860
How so?

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.800
Let's go, let's go!

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.910
There's no way ya don't know her!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.320
What's she angry about?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.320
She acted so close!

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.330
T-That must be 'cause 
we've met somewhere before.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.750
There, see?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.570
You <i>do</i> know her!

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:55.670
Haven't I been sayin' I don't?!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:59.550
If I had seen someone so gorgeous, even once before, 
how could I ever forget in the first place?

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.920
Someone... so gorgeous?

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.930
Well, I can't forget you, 
for an entirely different reason.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.050
<i>HUH?!</i>

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.930
What's that?! 
What d'ya mean by that?!

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:08.930
Hey, hey...

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.930
You really don't 
know this person, Heiji-niichan?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.300
Ooka... Momiji?

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:17.750
"High school champion of the Satsuki Cup for two consecutive years."

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.590
Second-year 
student at Senshin High...

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:23.820
"Viewed as certain to 
become the future queen."

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.840
Ooka Momiji?

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:28.320
The future queen?

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.330
Is this the advance 
notice you mentioned?

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.350
Yes.

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:34.710
It only says, 
"I will blow up Nichiuri TV".

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.020
What're these 
photos of karuta cards?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.330
They're photos that 
were attached to the email.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.460
We don't know 
what they mean yet.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.930
So? 
Does Nichiuri TV know about this?

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.990
We've issued them an alert, but...

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:49.640
What do you make of this, Heizo?

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:53.380
Is it a mere prank? 
Or a genuine bomb threat?

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:56.140
I cannot judge 
based on this email alone...

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:59.900
But if it's not a prank, 
this is a very serious matter.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.780
<i>Moments ago, the Osaka Prefectural Police issued us an official emergency evacuation warning.</i>

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.160
<i>All all operations and recording have been temporarily suspended...</i>

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.160
What's this creepy announcement?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.600
<i>Please vacate the premises via 
the nearest emergency staircase.</i>

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.410
What's this?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.650
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:13.540
Huh? Now there's 
an evacuation drill?!

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:13.540
<i>Moments ago...</i>

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.790
<i>The Osaka Prefectural Police issued us an official emergency evacuation warning.</i>

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.470
Is something starting?

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:16.790
It's saying "police", isn't it?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.790
Maybe they're 
recording something for TV.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.810
<i>All operations and recording 
have been temporarily suspended.</i>

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.800
<i>Please vacate the premises via 
the nearest emergency staircase.</i>

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.320
Hey, go look into this!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.130
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.080
What's going on here?

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:35.050
Kazuha, head for 
the fire escape now!

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:35.530
Got it?

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:36.770
W-What about you, Heiji?!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.280
I've gotta find 
out what happened!

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:40.810
You go 'n get 
outta here ahead of me!

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.480
Wait, Heiji!

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.590
Oh, come on...

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:47.760
That's dangerous!

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.040
Hey, boy!

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.390
Where're you trying to go?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.180
I forgot something in the studio.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:54.350
You idiot!

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.530
Couldn't you hear 
the announcement just now?!

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:57.220
Aw...

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.830
I do apologize.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.750
This is a first for me, as well.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.290
It's my first 
evacuation drill in a kimono.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.890
This is serious! 
We need to evacuate immediately!

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.680
Calm down. 
What happened?

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.850
I found out there was a 
threat to blow this place up!

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:12.670
What?!

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:13.680
Chairman Achiwa...

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.830
This may be false...

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.620
But until we confirm everyone's safety, we should evacuate for the time being!

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:18.730
Yes, you're right.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.100
Everyone, we're getting out, 
just as the announcement said!

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.020
Go on, hurry!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.210
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:29.150
What are ya doin', Mikiko-kun?

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.550
It's dangerous here. Hurry and go!

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.780
You too, Achiwa-san!

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.850
What're ya doin'?! 
Hurry 'n get out!

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.910
<i>Everyone, please move in an 
calm and orderly fashion.</i>

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:41.960
<i>There is nothing wrong. 
Everything's fine.</i>

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.310
You guys wait here, 
and don't move about, okay?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:45.880
<i>Now, once everyone has 
been confirmed safe...</i>

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.880
What? 
We gotta wait <i>again</i>?!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.160
It won't connect, after all.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.660
We left Dad behind, but is he okay?

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:53.010
Ran!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.970
Dad! Conan-kun!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.000
What on earth is going on here?

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.840
Don't tell me they're having an evacuation drill or something without any advance notice?!

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:00.450
Hey, Conan!

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:03.260
No...

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.480
We thought you were 
lost or something.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.110
I heard from one of 
the TV station staff before.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.110
O-Oh, yeah.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.980
They said this building 
received a bomb threat.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.980
What's wrong, Conan-kun?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.920
Oh, man. Really?

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:12.260
By the way, where's 
Kazuha-chan and Hattori-kun?

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:15.220
What? 
Weren't they with you all?

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:15.990
No...

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:18.330
I'm worried, so I'm 
going to go look for...

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.680
No, I'll go.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.540
Don't any of you 
move from this spot.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.990
Got it?!

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.160
Honestly!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.410
How could we be having an evacuation drill when we're so busy?!

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.430
This goes way 
too far for a joke.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.970
Ah, Heiji!

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.370
Mikiko!

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.390
Didn't I tell ya to 
go ahead and evacuate?!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:43.380
Yeah, ya did, but 
I was worried 'bout ya two...

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:47.880
Sorry, Kazuha.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.830
I can't leave those 
karuta cards behind, after all!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.470
If I calculate their position 
from their smartphone's GPS...

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.580
What?! Hattori's still inside?!

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.730
You there! 
What're you doing?

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.530
Forget those! 
Just hurry and evacuate!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:11.230
Honestly...

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.410
Mikiko!

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.410
Kazuha! 
 Hattori-kun!

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:17.070
Do you all know 
how dangerous this is?

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:18.080
I'm sorry!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.080
I'm sorry!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.240
Honestly...

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:24.130
I've taken three 
into care in studio three.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:25.510
Mikiko!

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.530
They all seem uninjured.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.220
This is really going too far!

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.560
I'm sorry.

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.560
<i>Then hurry and get them out of there.</i>

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.800
When I thought the 
bomb threat might be real...

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.270
Roger.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.070
It's like I couldn't stop myself.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.010
We don't know when 
the explosion will take place.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.700
We'll instruct everyone to keep their distance and be on alert.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.270
Please do.

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:44.180
He's begun evacuating the 
three who were still in the studio.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:45.930
Is that everyone?

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:46.330
Yes, sir.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:47.920
All right!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.660
We shall now begin searching 
for any suspicious objects.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.440
Begin heading in, men!

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:52.440
Roger!

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.970
We were in there! 
Is there really a bomb?!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.960
I bet it's a prank, anyhow.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.350
Come on, hurry!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.850
This way!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:12.440
Seriously?!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.510
Everyone, take cover!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:20.830
Men, fall back more! 
 Get away from the building!

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.320
Hurry, Mr. Chairman!

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:31.280
Watch out!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.400
Kazuha!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:37.960
Whoa!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.090
No! 
It's dangerous, so stay back!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:43.040
Damn it! 
Where'd they go?!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.320
It can't be...

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.350
You didn't get caught 
up in this, right, Hattori?!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.590
Kazuha!

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:50.840
You mustn't go! 
It's dangerous there.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.270
Okay, let's go.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.230
Ow...

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.280
Are you okay? Can you run?

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.220
Uh, yes.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.180
All right, then. 
Let's go. This way!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.840
We can't make it to the 
safe zone anymore, can we?

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.740
Indeed.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.240
Someone made it out again!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.240
Is there no one else left?

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.240
They said there 
are still two inside, so...

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:16.950
What?!

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.630
Kazuha, this way!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.200
Damn it!

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.560
Heiji!

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.290
That was close...

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.960
Take cover, take cover! 
Everyone get away!

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:38.130
So goin' down is out?

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:39.240
Kazuha, this way!

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.450
We're goin' up.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.060
What d'ya mean? 
We ain't goin' down?

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.540
If we can't get out, we've gotta get somewhere we can breathe first!

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.540
Wait, is Hattori...

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:53.040
Going up?!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.990
Damn. 
It really ain't connectin'?

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.000
Let's go, Kazuha!

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:08.630
Kazuha, this way!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.580
This roof ain't 
made of concrete?!

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.570
Closer! Get closer!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.260
We can't! 
 Any closer than this is dangerous!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.490
Sorry, let me through!

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.580
Damn!

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:32.460
I can't see anything 
through the smoke!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.600
I can't do this alone.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.150
If I <i>was</i> alone, that is!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.030
Kudo!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.340
Sink or swim...

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.620
I gotta do this.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.940
Go!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:03.990
Is that it?!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.560
So you've made 
your appearance, at last?

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.240
Hattori!

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.630
Wait... Heiji,  
where're we goin'?

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.680
Just come! 
This's the only way to get down now!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.460
Get down? But how?

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:32.660
We're gettin' down 
from here, Kazuha.

00:21:32.660 --> 00:21:33.170
Got it?

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:33.640
Heiji!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.270
Gettin' down from here? 
He's gotta be kidding!

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.170
Hey! 
We're ready, anytime!

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.690
Same here.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:40.840
There's no time. 
We'll all go at once.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:41.610
Right!

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:42.780
Kazuha!

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.250
We're really goin' from here?

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:45.790
Hey, I can't see in front...!

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.390
Heiji! 
Yer kiddin', right?!

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.220
Close your eyes, 'n hold on tight!

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:50.530
Wha...?! W-Wai...

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:52.350
Waitta sec!

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.760
No! 
Ya've gotta be kidding!

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.710
Sorry. 
We'll be waitin' down there ahead of ya.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.290
Come on, stop!

00:21:58.190 --> 00:21:59.190
Sure.

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:00.490
I can't close my eyes! 
I can't close my eyes!

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:01.840
I'm scared!

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:08.680
Kudo!

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:17.850
Damn it!

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:22.400
Kudo!

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:29.930
Impossible! 
Someone's over there!

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:31.830
Will you let go of me?!

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.140
Someone really <i>is </i>here!

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:34.830
Stretchers! 
Bring stretchers!

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:37.320
Kazuha?!

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:38.960
H-Heiji..?

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:46.590
Damn! That was the 
only place to get down, too!

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:50.640
There has to be another 
route out of here, somewhere.

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:53.080
A rescue helicopter!

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:56.600
No, that won't work. 
Not with all these flames and smoke.

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:59.040
Far from landing, 
it can't even get close!

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:02.590
Wait. 
There's a river next to this TV station!

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:04.270
If I can jump over to it...!

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:06.920
Alright!

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:09.320
Will this not work?

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:12.100
The foothold I need to pick up speed on my skateboard here is already gone.

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:15.640
Crap!

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:19.440
Just by taking a quick breath, 
my lungs feel like they're on fire!

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:20.950
I have to do something quickly!

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:22.990
If I don't...

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:30.200
Ran!

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:36.560
How could I just give up?!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.450
There has to still be one here!

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:42.220
Somewhere! A foothold to 
pick up speed on my skateboard!

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:43.520
That's it!

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:48.310
What're ya doin', Kudo? Hurry!

00:23:57.380 --> 00:23:58.830
That's...!

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:00.530
That's Kudo, no doubt.

00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:02.480
But what's he...?

00:24:04.190 --> 00:24:05.090
I get it!

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:06.840
So <i>that's</i> what yer doin'!

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:11.330
Faster!

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:13.770
Go faster!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:19.720
I can't breathe!

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.270
A little more! 
Just a little more!

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:26.340
Oh, no! It's falling!

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:29.600
This is as far as you go?!

00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:33.820
Damn! 
I didn't pick up enough speed?!

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:36.870
It's no use! 
I'll never make it!

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:43.360
I was waitin' for ya!

00:24:43.360 --> 00:24:45.000
And... gotcha!

00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:01.040
Are ya okay, Kudo?

00:25:01.950 --> 00:25:04.210
Yeah... Somehow.

00:25:04.210 --> 00:25:06.130
Here. 
You dropped these.

00:25:06.130 --> 00:25:07.420
Thank you.

00:25:07.420 --> 00:25:10.260
Anyway, for ya to have 
brought somethin' like that...

00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:13.150
Did ya know Nichiuri TV 
would be blown up?

00:25:13.150 --> 00:25:16.430
You idiot. 
Of course not...

00:25:16.430 --> 00:25:18.940
I had it, just in case.

00:25:18.940 --> 00:25:22.110
Ya sure ya didn't 
summon that "just in case"?

00:25:22.110 --> 00:25:25.370
Heh. 
Seems that way.

00:25:28.980 --> 00:25:30.480
Kazuha-chan!

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:31.250
Ran-chan!

00:25:31.810 --> 00:25:33.010
Were you okay?

00:25:33.010 --> 00:25:35.260
Yeah. 
I don't really remember it...

00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:38.250
But I only breathed in a bit of smoke.

00:25:38.250 --> 00:25:40.140
That's good, 
as long as you're fine.

00:25:40.670 --> 00:25:42.180
Anyway, thank goodness you're safe.

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:42.630
Yeah.

00:25:42.630 --> 00:25:45.650
Ran, it looks like I 
dropped the car keys somewhere...

00:25:45.650 --> 00:25:46.860
So I'm going to 
go look for them a bit.

00:25:46.860 --> 00:25:47.400
Okay.

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:49.630
Come to think of it, 
where's Conan-kun?

00:25:49.630 --> 00:25:52.840
Well, I thought he'd be 
at this evacuation area, but...

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:54.490
Hey! It's Conan!

00:25:54.490 --> 00:25:55.110
You're right!

00:25:55.110 --> 00:25:55.450
Conan-kun!

00:25:55.850 --> 00:25:57.220
Where did you go?

00:25:57.220 --> 00:25:58.440
We were worried about you!

00:25:58.440 --> 00:26:00.020
K-Kazuha!

00:26:00.020 --> 00:26:01.450
Hey, Heiji...

00:26:01.450 --> 00:26:03.300
Where'd ya go all this time?

00:26:03.310 --> 00:26:05.080
Oh, just somewhere.

00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:08.040
You too, Conan-kun! 
We were really worried about you!

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:09.360
I'm sorry.

00:26:09.360 --> 00:26:10.840
More importantly, where's Mikiko?

00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:15.090
Well, it seems she injured her arm somehow, and was taken to the hospital.

00:26:15.090 --> 00:26:16.280
Her arm...?

00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:18.840
It's great that her injury 
ain't more serious, but...

00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.290
I asked what 
hospital she was taken to...

00:26:21.290 --> 00:26:22.660
So how about 
we all go there now?

00:26:22.660 --> 00:26:24.380
Yeah! Let's go!

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:27.400
Hei-chan!

00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:28.290
Otaki-han!

00:26:28.290 --> 00:26:29.770
I'm so glad you're safe!

00:26:29.770 --> 00:26:32.480
Sorry, Kazuha, but 
you go on ahead of me.

00:26:32.480 --> 00:26:33.300
Wha...?!

00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:34.530
'Cause I'll be right behind you!

00:26:34.530 --> 00:26:35.400
Oh, come on...!

00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:37.100
Fine. 
Let's go, Ran-chan!

00:26:37.100 --> 00:26:39.780
Y-Yeah...
Come on, Conan-kun. We're going.

00:26:39.780 --> 00:26:41.200
S-Sure...

00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:43.090
No more getting separated now.

00:26:43.090 --> 00:26:43.810
Okay.

00:26:43.810 --> 00:26:45.950
See ya, Conan-kun!

00:26:47.180 --> 00:26:49.810
Did the police really get an advance notice about the bombs?

00:26:49.810 --> 00:26:52.710
This is the email 
that came to the police.

00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:56.340
Karuta cards were attached?

00:26:56.340 --> 00:27:01.210
This may have some connection to the recording of the karuta program.

00:27:01.210 --> 00:27:03.970
And with Nichiuri TV in that state...

00:27:03.970 --> 00:27:07.500
Seems like it'll take quite 
some time to inspect the site.

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:08.730
Right.

00:27:09.580 --> 00:27:13.940
What in the world is
 the bomber aiming for?

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:16.990
Naniwa Police Hospital

00:27:19.170 --> 00:27:21.140
Thank you for 
taking care of me.

00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.280
No problem. 
Take care of yourself.

00:27:22.280 --> 00:27:23.900
Mr. Chairman, how is it?

00:27:23.900 --> 00:27:26.860
It's nothing. 
Just a mere scratch.

00:27:26.860 --> 00:27:28.190
Thank goodness.

00:27:28.190 --> 00:27:31.700
To think we could get caught up in something like this right before the tournament...

00:27:31.700 --> 00:27:34.450
Yes. 
I never could have expected this.

00:27:34.450 --> 00:27:39.200
As it is, I may even have to discontinue the Satsuki Cup that's been held for many years.

00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:40.510
You mustn't!

00:27:41.040 --> 00:27:44.870
I feel that it's in times just like this that we need to emphasize the strength of the Satsuki Cup!

00:27:44.870 --> 00:27:50.060
But even the karuta cards used in the Satsuki Cup final were burned up.

00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:52.480
If that's all, then 
there's no need to worry.

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:53.790
The karuta cards are safe.

00:27:53.790 --> 00:27:54.110
What?

00:27:54.110 --> 00:27:55.390
What was that?

00:27:55.390 --> 00:27:56.660
W-What do you mean?

00:27:56.660 --> 00:27:59.890
During evacuation, 
Hiramoto-san took them out with her.

00:27:59.890 --> 00:28:01.700
M-Mikiko-kun did?!

00:28:01.700 --> 00:28:05.260
Far from being burnt, 
the karuta were safe, somehow!

00:28:05.260 --> 00:28:06.120
Is that true?!

00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:08.700
Are the Satsuki Cup 
karuta cards really safe?

00:28:09.140 --> 00:28:11.330
To check whether 
they were damaged or not...

00:28:11.330 --> 00:28:13.960
They were taken by the museum staff.

00:28:13.960 --> 00:28:17.110
Mr. Chairman, 
the karuta cards are fine.

00:28:17.110 --> 00:28:18.530
Please rest assured of that.

00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:22.220
I thought they were ruined, but that's great.

00:28:22.220 --> 00:28:26.750
So Mikiko-kun saved the 
Satsuki Cup karuta cards, but how is she?

00:28:26.750 --> 00:28:29.720
Though I hear it's 
nothing life-threatening...

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:32.420
It seems she's still being examined.

00:28:32.420 --> 00:28:33.600
I see.

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:36.090
Mikiko-chan's 
taking a while, isn't she?

00:28:36.090 --> 00:28:39.340
The doctor said they'd only 
be doin' some first aid on her...

00:28:39.340 --> 00:28:41.140
Thank you.

00:28:41.140 --> 00:28:42.250
Mikiko!

00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:44.240
Don't tell me your arm's...

00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:46.810
Yeah. 
It seems it's broken.

00:28:48.180 --> 00:28:49.740
I got what I deserved.

00:28:49.740 --> 00:28:50.750
No way..

00:28:50.750 --> 00:28:55.150
By going back to get the karuta cards, 
I put you and Hattori-kun in danger, Kazuha...

00:28:55.150 --> 00:28:56.320
What're ya talkin' about?!

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:58.250
Thank you, Mikiko-kun.

00:28:58.250 --> 00:29:02.660
You saved the karuta cards that are also called the face of the Satsuki Cup.

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:07.350
As the representative of the Cup, 
I must express my feelings of gratitude.

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:11.290
But, Mr. Chairman!
I can't play in the Satsuki Cup like this!

00:29:11.290 --> 00:29:12.060
Indeed.

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:18.360
It is immensely unfortunate for the Satsuki Cup that someone of your caliber is unable to participate.

00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:21.760
But for now, I think it's best for you to focus on your injuries healing.

00:29:21.760 --> 00:29:23.280
That's right.

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:25.440
Ain't there another 
competition next year?

00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:26.690
That won't work!

00:29:26.690 --> 00:29:27.030
Huh?

00:29:27.030 --> 00:29:30.690
If we don't get a good 
ranking in this year's Satsuki Cup...

00:29:30.690 --> 00:29:32.580
The club will 
end up being disbanded.

00:29:32.580 --> 00:29:36.570
I just can't let the karuta 
club end with my generation...

00:29:36.570 --> 00:29:37.370
Mr. Chairman.

00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:40.840
The police are waiting. 
We should go soon.

00:29:40.840 --> 00:29:41.510
Right.

00:29:41.510 --> 00:29:43.330
Cheer up, Mikiko.

00:29:43.330 --> 00:29:44.830
Yeah, but...

00:29:44.830 --> 00:29:47.340
Frankly, it's true that 
other than you and me, Mikiko...

00:29:47.340 --> 00:29:50.350
There weren't any other members who can play karuta as well.

00:29:50.350 --> 00:29:51.550
That's it, Kazuha!

00:29:51.550 --> 00:29:52.520
You go out and play!

00:29:52.970 --> 00:29:55.850
In my stead, as the 
representative of Kaiho Academy!

00:29:55.850 --> 00:29:58.170
Asking me out 
of the blue like that...

00:29:58.170 --> 00:30:00.590
Have you ever appeared 
in the tournament, Kazuha-chan?

00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:01.340
No, never!

00:30:01.360 --> 00:30:04.210
But you always went 
with me to my practices, right?

00:30:04.210 --> 00:30:04.850
Yeah...

00:30:04.850 --> 00:30:08.540
You have tip-top stamina, 
and sharp reflexes, Kazuha-chan!

00:30:08.550 --> 00:30:12.060
You're strong-willed and competitive, 
never giving in, no matter the opponent!

00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:14.820
And aren't ya 
unusually thick-skinned?

00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:17.690
I don't really feel like 
I'm bein' complimented...

00:30:17.690 --> 00:30:20.070
When's the competition?

00:30:20.070 --> 00:30:22.260
It's the day after tomorrow.

00:30:22.260 --> 00:30:22.500
What?!

00:30:22.500 --> 00:30:23.780
You'll be fine!

00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:27.010
Things will work out if we start giving you special training now, Kazuha!

00:30:29.030 --> 00:30:32.140
An amateur's entering the 
competition and aiming to win?

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:36.930
The game of karuta is based on the "Hyakunin Isshu", 
a classic collection of 100 poems, each written by a different poet. 
"Iroha Karuta" is a simplified children's version.

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:36.930
Rather than the <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i>-based cards, 
should we have them swap in the <i>Iroha Karuta</i> for you?

00:30:36.930 --> 00:30:38.740
Don't make fun of her!

00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:42.360
I know Kazuha's skills the most, from how she's always practicing!

00:30:43.050 --> 00:30:44.420
She doesn't have any 
experience in competitions...

00:30:44.420 --> 00:30:46.640
But there's no doubt her 
skills match that of A-class!

00:30:46.640 --> 00:30:47.780
Oh?

00:30:48.550 --> 00:30:50.530
Is she now?

00:30:50.530 --> 00:30:54.570
Come to think of it, 
you were with Heiji-kun...

00:30:54.570 --> 00:30:56.730
But what relationship 
do you have with him?

00:30:56.730 --> 00:30:59.680
We've always been together, 
ever since we were little!

00:30:59.680 --> 00:31:01.280
Heiji's my...!

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:02.480
My...

00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:04.300
You really like him, don't you?

00:31:04.910 --> 00:31:06.350
We can tell just by looking.

00:31:06.350 --> 00:31:07.090
It's totally obvious!

00:31:07.090 --> 00:31:08.840
Keep your mouths shut!

00:31:08.840 --> 00:31:10.960
"Though I try to hide it..." 
Am I right?

00:31:12.260 --> 00:31:14.760
Childhood friends playing lovers...

00:31:14.760 --> 00:31:17.460
Honestly, that puts me at ease.

00:31:18.420 --> 00:31:19.920
In that case, 
how about we do this?

00:31:19.920 --> 00:31:24.770
The winner of tomorrow's competition will become the top candidate to be Heiji-kun's wife.

00:31:24.770 --> 00:31:27.530
She'll get to confess their 
feelings first and win Heiji-kun.

00:31:27.530 --> 00:31:29.030
So, how about it?

00:31:29.030 --> 00:31:31.630
Hey, what're ya saying?

00:31:31.630 --> 00:31:35.410
If you're really serious about him, you're prepared to do that much, aren't you?

00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:38.990
Kazuha, don't 
accept such a challenge!

00:31:38.990 --> 00:31:40.330
I'll say this in advance...

00:31:40.980 --> 00:31:42.850
But I'm serious.

00:31:46.110 --> 00:31:47.450
Wait!

00:31:47.460 --> 00:31:49.930
I accept your challenge!

00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:52.410
K-Kazuha-chan!

00:31:52.410 --> 00:31:53.160
Seriously?!

00:31:53.490 --> 00:31:57.540
It'll be great if you can hold onto that energy until the day of the match.

00:31:57.540 --> 00:31:59.050
Same goes for ya!

00:31:59.050 --> 00:32:01.040
Ya better not lose 
before ya face me!

00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:04.370
In that case, 
I'll be taking my leave now.

00:32:04.370 --> 00:32:08.730
Because I've gotta think of the right words to confess my feelings to Heiji-kun while I'm at the nail salon.

00:32:12.490 --> 00:32:14.680
That lady seems scary, doesn't she?

00:32:14.680 --> 00:32:15.140
Yes...

00:32:15.140 --> 00:32:16.490
We saw sure saw
something amazing, didn't we?

00:32:16.490 --> 00:32:18.980
You really <i>are</i> incredible!

00:32:18.980 --> 00:32:21.250
To think you could
go against Momiji so fiercely!

00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:22.570
What do I do?

00:32:22.570 --> 00:32:23.210
Huh?

00:32:23.210 --> 00:32:25.250
I made a terrible promise.

00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:30.990
I'm very sorry.

00:32:30.990 --> 00:32:32.050
No, It's my fault.

00:32:32.700 --> 00:32:34.660
Dad! 
Did you find the keys?

00:32:34.660 --> 00:32:36.370
Well, about that...

00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:39.320
I looked all over the place, 
but couldn't find them.

00:32:39.320 --> 00:32:40.520
What...?!

00:32:40.520 --> 00:32:43.040
At this rate, all we 
can do is make a spare key.

00:32:43.040 --> 00:32:45.100
Oh? 
What's wrong, Conan-kun?

00:32:45.100 --> 00:32:48.380
It looks like the lady 
from before dropped this.

00:32:48.380 --> 00:32:51.110
What? 
Let me see it.

00:32:51.110 --> 00:32:53.110
You're right. 
This is Momiji-san's.

00:32:53.110 --> 00:32:55.060
Dad, I'm going 
to go get this to her!

00:32:55.060 --> 00:32:56.120
Hey, do you know her?

00:32:56.120 --> 00:32:58.000
This's really 
bringin' me down.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:32:59.640
What d'ya think I should do?!

00:32:59.640 --> 00:33:01.110
"What should you do...?"

00:33:01.110 --> 00:33:03.000
She seemed kinda scary...

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.810
But she was 
really pretty, wasn't she?!

00:33:04.810 --> 00:33:08.750
If Heiji-san's confessed to by someone like that, he'll be head over heels...

00:33:09.660 --> 00:33:12.430
B-But you're the only 
good match for him, Kazuha-san!

00:33:12.430 --> 00:33:13.130
Really?!

00:33:13.130 --> 00:33:14.630
Really, really!

00:33:15.160 --> 00:33:17.380
This's no time to be 
grumbling 'bout something like this!

00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:19.380
We're havin' all-night 
special training tonight!

00:33:22.010 --> 00:33:24.640
This's the first time 
I've been to a hospital!

00:33:24.640 --> 00:33:27.050
It's so big! 
I could get lost in here!

00:33:27.050 --> 00:33:28.770
Ran-neechan... 
There she is, over there!

00:33:28.770 --> 00:33:30.270
Momiji-san!

00:33:30.270 --> 00:33:31.480
Wait a second!

00:33:33.300 --> 00:33:35.280
Wait, Momiji-san!

00:33:35.280 --> 00:33:38.500
Aw... She left.

00:33:38.500 --> 00:33:39.660
What should we do with this?

00:33:39.660 --> 00:33:41.810
We know her name and school...

00:33:41.810 --> 00:33:44.650
But wouldn't it be quicker to 
look inside for some contact info?

00:33:44.650 --> 00:33:45.790
You're right.

00:33:46.490 --> 00:33:48.250
Ran-neechan, let me see, too!

00:33:48.250 --> 00:33:49.240
Oh, sure...

00:33:49.240 --> 00:33:52.050
Let's see... 
Oh, it's a photo?

00:33:52.050 --> 00:33:54.800
Who is that man?

00:33:54.800 --> 00:33:56.790
Oh, there's one more.

00:33:56.790 --> 00:33:57.800
Wha...?

00:33:58.660 --> 00:34:00.580
It looks like it's a photo 
from when she was a child...

00:34:00.580 --> 00:34:02.670
That's Momiji-san and...

00:34:02.670 --> 00:34:04.580
...Hattori-kun, isn't it?

00:34:04.580 --> 00:34:06.230
They're making a 
pinky promise, aren't they?

00:34:08.120 --> 00:34:10.130
I wonder what promise they made?

00:34:10.130 --> 00:34:11.970
A promise to get 
married, or something?

00:34:13.650 --> 00:34:14.940
When they're just kids?

00:34:14.940 --> 00:34:16.680
That couldn't 
possibly be it, could it?

00:34:16.680 --> 00:34:17.620
No...

00:34:17.620 --> 00:34:19.910
He can be 
awfully careless, so...

00:34:19.910 --> 00:34:21.240
<b>That might be it.</b>

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:26.270
Oh, hey! 
That's Heiji-niichan's motorcycle!

00:34:26.270 --> 00:34:28.670
Make <i>absolutely </i>sure you 
keep that photo a secret, okay?

00:34:30.250 --> 00:34:31.950
Especially from Kazuha-chan.

00:34:31.950 --> 00:34:32.750
Right.

00:34:39.240 --> 00:34:41.540
What's this? 
Ya two're here to greet me?

00:34:41.540 --> 00:34:42.930
No...

00:34:44.260 --> 00:34:46.000
What's up with her?

00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:47.230
Ran!

00:34:47.230 --> 00:34:48.620
Were you able to give 
her what she dropped?

00:34:48.620 --> 00:34:50.010
Oh. 
Uh, yeah...

00:34:50.010 --> 00:34:50.840
Hey.

00:34:50.840 --> 00:34:52.010
You sure took a while.

00:34:52.920 --> 00:34:54.690
Did you find out anything?

00:34:54.690 --> 00:34:58.520
No, the Osaka Prefectural 
Police're still in disarray.

00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:02.230
Otaki-han's gonna contact 
me once he gathers some info.

00:35:02.230 --> 00:35:05.270
Mr. Chairman, regarding 
that urgent matter I mentioned...

00:35:05.270 --> 00:35:07.400
Could we have you answer this call?

00:35:07.400 --> 00:35:08.780
Sure, I don't mind.

00:35:08.780 --> 00:35:09.710
Honestly!

00:35:09.710 --> 00:35:12.240
What's going on with Ran?!

00:35:09.710 --> 00:35:11.370
Yes. What is it?!

00:35:12.240 --> 00:35:14.210
From the Kyoto Prefectural Police?!

00:35:14.210 --> 00:35:15.700
Yes.

00:35:15.700 --> 00:35:18.370
And what about Yajima-kun?

00:35:18.370 --> 00:35:20.340
What? 
He was killed?!

00:35:21.510 --> 00:35:22.190
Hattori!

00:35:22.190 --> 00:35:22.960
Right.

00:35:22.190 --> 00:35:22.960
I understand.

00:35:22.960 --> 00:35:25.850
I'll cancel everything 
and be right there.

00:35:22.960 --> 00:35:25.850
Hey, stop! 
Wait, you two!

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:32.840
Thank you for all your work.

00:35:35.630 --> 00:35:38.800
Look, you two. 
This place is off limits.

00:35:38.800 --> 00:35:41.030
We're with Mouri Kogoro.

00:35:41.030 --> 00:35:42.670
What idiotic things are you saying?!!

00:35:42.670 --> 00:35:45.140
I don't mind you 
lettin' those kids through.

00:35:45.140 --> 00:35:45.910
O-Oh, right.

00:35:45.910 --> 00:35:48.290
It's been quite a while, you two.

00:35:48.290 --> 00:35:51.290
Inspector Ayanokouji!

00:35:51.760 --> 00:35:54.160
The murder victim 
is Yajima Toshiya-san.

00:35:54.160 --> 00:35:56.120
He's the son of a 
wealthy brewery family.

00:35:56.120 --> 00:35:58.300
And seems to have 
lived in this mansion alone.

00:35:58.790 --> 00:36:01.570
His time of death is presumed to have been around six this morning.

00:36:01.570 --> 00:36:04.300
His body was discovered 
eight hours later, at 2 PM.

00:36:04.300 --> 00:36:07.460
Oh, please watch your step.

00:36:07.460 --> 00:36:09.430
There's a great 
amount of damage done.

00:36:09.430 --> 00:36:10.810
Y-Yeah...

00:36:10.810 --> 00:36:11.940
You say this was a robbery?

00:36:11.940 --> 00:36:14.000
Based on the state 
of the crime scene...

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:16.210
I'd say it's certain 
this was a robbery-murder.

00:36:16.210 --> 00:36:19.190
Indeed. 
We believe that, as well.

00:36:19.190 --> 00:36:22.260
Someone breaks in, 
seeking money or valuables...

00:36:22.260 --> 00:36:24.600
And came across Yajima-san.

00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:28.980
So in that instant, the murderer used the Japanese sword they were trying to steal to club him to death...

00:36:28.980 --> 00:36:31.710
Took any money, 
and fled afterwards.

00:36:31.710 --> 00:36:34.070
But why...? Why?

00:36:34.070 --> 00:36:37.320
From the look of things, it seems the victim had been playing karuta.

00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:38.650
Sure does.

00:36:39.090 --> 00:36:41.300
How did <i>you two</i> get in here?

00:36:41.300 --> 00:36:42.910
So, Inspector...

00:36:42.910 --> 00:36:45.550
We'll look over 
the crime scene a bit.

00:36:45.550 --> 00:36:49.060
Forensics have already finished their work here, so do as you please.

00:36:49.200 --> 00:36:50.880
Wha...? They can?

00:36:50.880 --> 00:36:55.170
However, as it is the weapon, we shall be collecting the sword.

00:36:55.170 --> 00:36:56.650
Sure. 
We don't mind.

00:36:56.650 --> 00:37:00.330
Please accompany those 
two until they're satisfied.

00:37:00.330 --> 00:37:01.050
Yes, sir.

00:37:01.050 --> 00:37:03.030
Then, I shall be waiting outside.

00:37:03.030 --> 00:37:05.430
Please tell me 
if you find out anything.

00:37:05.430 --> 00:37:06.690
Sure.

00:37:09.160 --> 00:37:10.530
What d'ya think?

00:37:10.530 --> 00:37:12.870
I can't say anything for sure yet...

00:37:12.870 --> 00:37:14.260
But his right hand...

00:37:14.260 --> 00:37:16.490
Yeah. 
So ya realized that too, Kudo?

00:37:16.490 --> 00:37:17.570
Yeah.

00:37:17.570 --> 00:37:20.550
It gives the feeling that someone forcibly removed something that had blood on it.

00:37:21.070 --> 00:37:23.420
When you say something 
in the room with blood on it...

00:37:23.420 --> 00:37:25.160
A karuta card?

00:37:25.160 --> 00:37:27.700
The murderer, who 
figured out his dying message...

00:37:27.700 --> 00:37:30.180
Mixed the card into the other cards that were scattered around.

00:37:30.180 --> 00:37:33.300
It'll be impossible to find 
that card outta all of these.

00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:35.310
In that case, leave it to me.

00:37:35.310 --> 00:37:37.810
There's someone who's 
good at this kind of analysis.

00:37:39.340 --> 00:37:40.630
Oh, what's that?

00:37:41.420 --> 00:37:43.470
Seeing how that 
remote has blood on it...

00:37:43.470 --> 00:37:45.320
It should have been 
right next to the victim, but...

00:37:46.360 --> 00:37:47.740
Excuse me.

00:37:47.740 --> 00:37:49.470
It it okay if we lift that TV up?

00:37:49.470 --> 00:37:50.930
Yes, go ahead.

00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:51.660
Thanks.

00:37:51.660 --> 00:37:55.290
If he was usin' the remote 
right before he was killed...

00:37:55.290 --> 00:37:56.690
There might be 
somethin' on screen.

00:37:58.980 --> 00:38:00.290
It's Ooka Momiji.

00:38:00.290 --> 00:38:04.050
So Yajima-san was watching this right up until he was attacked?

00:38:04.690 --> 00:38:05.670
What's wrong?

00:38:05.670 --> 00:38:07.950
It looks to be a past game...

00:38:07.950 --> 00:38:09.160
Yeah.

00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:14.250
"The 15th to 20th Annual High School Satsuki Cup Competitions."

00:38:14.740 --> 00:38:16.920
Why was Yajima-san 
watching this video?

00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:20.840
Because it is an appropriately high-level match, being the final.

00:38:20.840 --> 00:38:23.760
From performance strategy,
 to how the cards are lined up...

00:38:23.760 --> 00:38:26.740
There is much that can be used as a reference, even just by watching.

00:38:26.740 --> 00:38:29.620
It does not have any 
relation to this murder.

00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:31.910
15th-20th Annual
High School Satsuki Cup
Competitions

00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:30.640
Oh, but...

00:38:30.640 --> 00:38:33.100
Shut up with your "buts"!

00:38:33.100 --> 00:38:34.830
Hey! 
You're coming, too!

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:36.730
Enough playing detectives!

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:36.730
W-Wait! Oww...

00:38:36.730 --> 00:38:39.080
Thanks, everyone. 
Sorry for causing you trouble.

00:38:36.730 --> 00:38:37.970
What're ya doin'?!

00:38:37.970 --> 00:38:39.080
Oww!

00:38:39.080 --> 00:38:41.380
Put me down, Uncle!

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:40.660
Not a problem.

00:38:41.380 --> 00:38:43.590
We get it! 
We get it, so let go of us!

00:38:48.090 --> 00:38:49.990
<i>Continuing with the news...</i>

00:38:49.990 --> 00:38:51.250
<i>At around 1 PM today...</i>

00:38:51.250 --> 00:38:54.910
This news story again? 
It sure is worrying.

00:38:54.910 --> 00:38:57.730
Oh? 
Why did you turn it off, Ai-kun?

00:38:57.730 --> 00:39:02.050
You won't remain healthy if you worry every time this news story comes up.

00:39:02.050 --> 00:39:03.210
Yes, but...

00:39:03.210 --> 00:39:05.360
You got in touch 
with the kids, correct?

00:39:05.360 --> 00:39:09.490
But I haven't gotten a 
call back from Shinichi...

00:39:09.490 --> 00:39:09.860
Oh?

00:39:11.690 --> 00:39:12.120
See?

00:39:12.770 --> 00:39:13.990
Speak of the devil.

00:39:13.990 --> 00:39:16.190
Oh! Pass me the 
phone after you're done!

00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:17.410
Sure.

00:39:17.410 --> 00:39:21.420
Um, what in the world were you doing, without even contacting us?!

00:39:21.420 --> 00:39:23.850
<i>The professor's 
really   worried, you know!</i>

00:39:23.850 --> 00:39:24.990
Sorry, sorry.

00:39:24.990 --> 00:39:26.800
We had all kinds of 
problems on our end, too.

00:39:26.800 --> 00:39:28.660
<i>So, what do you need?</i>

00:39:28.660 --> 00:39:31.720
I sent some photos 
to your computer earlier...

00:39:31.720 --> 00:39:35.600
But I'd like you to look into
the karuta cards in those photos.

00:39:35.600 --> 00:39:38.340
Just when we thought you 
got caught up in the bombing...

00:39:38.340 --> 00:39:40.350
Now you have 
blood-stained karuta cards?

00:39:40.350 --> 00:39:44.400
I want you to determine which of those cards the victim had been holding onto.

00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:47.800
<i>Aren't you good at persistently 
piecing things like that together?</i>

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:49.280
"Persistently", huh?

00:39:49.280 --> 00:39:49.700
Oh?

00:39:50.550 --> 00:39:52.850
There's a photo of 
someone in one of these.

00:39:52.850 --> 00:39:53.760
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:39:53.760 --> 00:39:56.450
<i>While you're at it, 
could you look into him too?</i>

00:39:56.450 --> 00:39:58.100
Does this guy also 
have a connection to karuta?

00:39:58.100 --> 00:40:00.270
<i>Well, I suspect he does.</i>

00:40:01.250 --> 00:40:04.270
<i>I'll try, anyhow, 
so give me a little time.</i>

00:40:04.270 --> 00:40:06.050
Thanks! 
I'm relying on you!

00:40:06.050 --> 00:40:06.910
<i>Later!</i>

00:40:06.910 --> 00:40:08.580
Wait a second! 
The professor wants...

00:40:09.400 --> 00:40:10.800
That's just dirty...

00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:15.000
In that case, it's the main members in the Satsuki Cup that're being targeted.

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:17.310
Right. 
Two are certain to be marked.

00:40:17.310 --> 00:40:19.180
I'll keep watch over Achiwa-san.

00:40:19.180 --> 00:40:22.060
If I recall, we should be 
staying at the same hotel.

00:40:22.060 --> 00:40:24.960
Then I'll take Ooka Momiji.

00:40:26.210 --> 00:40:29.060
Hold it! Hold it! 
What do you need?

00:40:29.060 --> 00:40:31.570
I'm part of the Satsuki Cup. 
Let me through.

00:40:31.570 --> 00:40:34.640
Please wait. 
We'll confirm that now.

00:40:34.640 --> 00:40:35.570
Sekine-kun!

00:40:35.570 --> 00:40:38.340
What were you 
doing all this time?

00:40:38.340 --> 00:40:40.110
Didn't I call you 
over and over again?

00:40:40.110 --> 00:40:41.370
I'm sorry, Mr. Chairman.

00:40:41.370 --> 00:40:43.440
I drank too much last night...

00:40:43.440 --> 00:40:47.150
And I fell asleep without realizing my phone's batteries had died.

00:40:47.150 --> 00:40:48.300
Good grief.

00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:50.240
And when I woke up...

00:40:50.240 --> 00:40:53.300
The news was sayin' the 
TV station was blown up...

00:40:53.300 --> 00:40:57.710
And when I contacted the Cup staff, they said you were looking for me at Yajima-san's place.

00:40:57.710 --> 00:41:00.060
Now, when I get here, 
there's this big commotion...

00:41:00.620 --> 00:41:02.220
And all these cops are gathered here.

00:41:02.220 --> 00:41:03.810
Did something happen to Yajima-san?

00:41:03.810 --> 00:41:07.650
Yajima-kun... was killed.

00:41:07.650 --> 00:41:08.960
What...?!

00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:11.680
Apparently, it happened 
as part of a robbery...

00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:13.680
With the sword he had 
hanging in the corridor.

00:41:13.680 --> 00:41:14.780
With a sword...?

00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:15.930
No way...

00:41:15.930 --> 00:41:18.140
Achiwa-san, 
who might this be?

00:41:18.140 --> 00:41:19.580
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:41:19.580 --> 00:41:24.080
My name is Sekine Kouji.
I'm working as the cameraman of the Satsuki Cup.

00:41:24.620 --> 00:41:27.320
Sekine-kun was Yajima-kun's rival...

00:41:27.320 --> 00:41:31.340
And for the past two years, the Satsuki Cup final was a competition between those two.

00:41:31.340 --> 00:41:33.530
Well, I lost two years in a row...

00:41:33.530 --> 00:41:36.340
And had thought 
this would be my year...

00:41:36.340 --> 00:41:39.600
But now I can never 
compete against him again, can I?

00:41:39.600 --> 00:41:43.620
So are you going to 
hold the competition as planned?

00:41:43.620 --> 00:41:47.170
Actually, I'm not sure 
what I should do about that.

00:41:47.170 --> 00:41:48.920
Ya can't give it up, Mr. Chairman.

00:41:48.920 --> 00:41:52.230
If the legendary Satsuki Cup was discontinued because of Yajima's death...

00:41:52.230 --> 00:41:54.600
Wouldn't that mean 
Yajima died in vain?

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:55.880
I mean, wasn't he beaten down?!

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:59.160
Sekine-kun! 
Show some discretion in your words!

00:41:59.160 --> 00:41:59.740
No, uh...

00:41:59.740 --> 00:42:01.730
I'm sorry, 
that just slipped out.

00:42:01.730 --> 00:42:03.770
I am part of the 
Kyoto Prefectural Police.

00:42:03.770 --> 00:42:08.360
I have two or three things we would ask you, 
but may I have a few moments of your time?

00:42:08.360 --> 00:42:10.990
Oh, yeah. Of course. 
I'll answer whatever you need.

00:42:10.990 --> 00:42:12.200
Then, come this way.

00:42:12.200 --> 00:42:13.170
Yes, okay.

00:42:13.170 --> 00:42:14.590
Mouri-san...

00:42:14.590 --> 00:42:17.340
I need to return to Osaka soon.

00:42:14.590 --> 00:42:16.120
Hey, Kudo.

00:42:16.120 --> 00:42:18.160
I know who the killer is.

00:42:17.340 --> 00:42:18.440
Yes, of course.

00:42:18.160 --> 00:42:19.680
So do I.

00:42:18.440 --> 00:42:19.680
I'll guide you.

00:42:19.680 --> 00:42:22.620
<i>He </i>must be Yajima-san's killer.

00:42:22.620 --> 00:42:25.400
But considering that 
the Satsuki Cup was targeted...

00:42:25.400 --> 00:42:28.960
I still can't understand his crime of blowing up the TV station...

00:42:28.960 --> 00:42:30.190
I know.

00:42:30.190 --> 00:42:35.340
Ain't it safer to keep watch over Achiwa-san and Momiji like we decided earlier?

00:42:35.340 --> 00:42:36.950
Yeah.

00:42:39.110 --> 00:42:40.950
Hotel
New Otani

00:42:41.370 --> 00:42:42.440
I'm first!

00:42:42.440 --> 00:42:43.450
I'm second!

00:42:43.450 --> 00:42:46.290
No fair, you two! 
Wait for me!

00:42:46.290 --> 00:42:48.940
Whoa! 
What a super spacious room!

00:42:48.940 --> 00:42:51.230
Sonoko reserved it for us.

00:42:51.230 --> 00:42:54.280
Remember? Wasn't even Sonoko brimming with excitement about coming?

00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:58.090
That's apparently why she chose a hotel close to Nichiuri TV for us.

00:42:58.090 --> 00:43:00.410
That's the Suzuki Financial Group, for ya!

00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:02.830
Oh, is that right?

00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:07.980
I hear they're also going to doing special training all night, so prepare dinner for them, too.

00:43:07.980 --> 00:43:09.840
Then, please do.

00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:13.920
Oh, why did this 
have to happen to me?

00:43:14.420 --> 00:43:18.610
To see you, cheering on your 
friend with everything you have...

00:43:20.340 --> 00:43:22.120
Oh, well.

00:43:22.120 --> 00:43:24.120
Now, let's start 
our special training!

00:43:24.120 --> 00:43:25.800
We'll help, too!

00:43:25.800 --> 00:43:28.250
Tell us if there's 
anything we can do!

00:43:28.250 --> 00:43:30.340
We will completely back you up!

00:43:30.340 --> 00:43:31.250
You guys!

00:43:31.250 --> 00:43:32.610
Really? 
Thanks a lot!

00:43:33.370 --> 00:43:34.250
It's my phone.

00:43:34.250 --> 00:43:35.650
Who's it from?

00:43:35.650 --> 00:43:36.650
It's from the professor.

00:43:36.650 --> 00:43:38.030
Ayumi wants to talk, too!

00:43:38.030 --> 00:43:39.510
Let's all talk to him!

00:43:39.510 --> 00:43:40.910
Yes, let's do that!

00:43:40.910 --> 00:43:43.460
Good luck with the 
special training, ladies.

00:43:43.460 --> 00:43:46.010
We'll be over there, 
so we won't bother you!

00:43:46.910 --> 00:43:49.460
By "completely backing us up"...

00:43:49.460 --> 00:43:50.840
<i>This</i> is what they meant?

00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:53.460
<i>Oh, it's on! It's on!</i>

00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:55.770
<i>You all haven't had anything 
else happen since then, have you?</i>

00:43:55.770 --> 00:43:56.670
Nope!

00:43:56.670 --> 00:43:57.680
We've been fine!

00:43:57.680 --> 00:43:59.140
We're already at the hotel!

00:43:59.140 --> 00:44:01.130
<i>I see. 
That's perfect.</i>

00:44:01.130 --> 00:44:01.620
Wha...?

00:44:01.620 --> 00:44:02.140
It couldn't be...

00:44:02.140 --> 00:44:04.450
<i>Ta-da! 
Now for what you've all been waiting for...</i>

00:44:04.450 --> 00:44:06.790
"The Professor's Quiz Corner!"

00:44:07.390 --> 00:44:09.610
Is <i>that </i>what you called us for?

00:44:09.610 --> 00:44:11.280
<i>I'll keep the call short.</i>

00:44:11.280 --> 00:44:14.290
<i>The unique style 
of competitive karuta...</i>

00:44:14.290 --> 00:44:17.870
<i>Is said to resemble that of a 
type of traditional Japanese work...</i>

00:44:17.870 --> 00:44:19.950
<i>But which of the following is it?</i>

00:44:19.950 --> 00:44:21.660
<i>1. Tea leaf harvesting.</i>

00:44:21.660 --> 00:44:23.500
<i>2. Kite flying.</i>

00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:25.420
<i>3. Mochi pounding.</i>

00:44:25.420 --> 00:44:27.680
<i>4. Rice harvesting.</i>

00:44:27.680 --> 00:44:31.450
You take cards and pile them up, so maybe it's tea leaf harvesting?

00:44:31.450 --> 00:44:32.790
Is it kite flying?

00:44:32.770 --> 00:44:34.520
I wanna eat some octopus balls!

00:44:34.520 --> 00:44:35.810
You can "touch the wrong card"...

00:44:35.810 --> 00:44:36.940
So is it "mochi pounding"?

00:44:36.940 --> 00:44:38.960
<i>Is that your final answer?</i>

00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:41.090
<i>The answer is 4, rice harvesting.</i>

00:44:41.090 --> 00:44:41.610
<i>Ai-kun!</i>

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:43.300
<i>Rice plants 
become paddy fields...</i>

00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:44.820
<i>And "once you cut" those paddy fields...</i>

00:44:44.810 --> 00:44:45.530
Oh!

00:44:45.530 --> 00:44:46.650
It's karuta!

00:44:47.680 --> 00:44:49.850
<i>I see you may lack 
any sense of warmth or fun..</i>

00:44:49.850 --> 00:44:51.120
<i>You guys...</i>

00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:54.120
Don't stay up too late, 
just because you're on a trip!

00:44:54.120 --> 00:44:55.490
<i>We won't!</i>

00:44:56.750 --> 00:44:58.070
<i>Then, I'm hanging up now.</i>

00:44:58.070 --> 00:44:59.280
Okay!

00:44:59.280 --> 00:45:01.720
It was this late already?

00:45:01.720 --> 00:45:04.450
So much happened today, didn't it?

00:45:02.740 --> 00:45:04.450
Dad and the 
others sure are late.

00:45:04.450 --> 00:45:06.510
I wonder if Heiji's 
still with them, too.

00:45:06.510 --> 00:45:09.390
If you're that worried, 
why not try calling him?

00:45:09.390 --> 00:45:11.830
Y-Yeah, you're right...

00:45:16.910 --> 00:45:18.210
What's up, Kazuha?

00:45:18.210 --> 00:45:19.440
<i>What d'ya mean, "what's up"?</i>

00:45:19.440 --> 00:45:22.390
Where're ya wanderin' 
about this late at night?

00:45:22.390 --> 00:45:23.800
Huh? Kyoto?

00:45:23.800 --> 00:45:25.060
What's goin' on?

00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:26.260
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:45:26.260 --> 00:45:28.240
<i>Some minor business came up, 
and I don't think I can see him off today...</i>

00:45:28.240 --> 00:45:29.200
<i>So you head home ahead of me.</i>

00:45:29.560 --> 00:45:31.080
What's that?

00:45:31.080 --> 00:45:33.710
I thought I'd have ya join us for the special karuta training, too!

00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:34.650
Special training?

00:45:34.650 --> 00:45:38.860
<i>I'm gonna be in the 
karuta match in place of Mikiko!</i>

00:45:38.860 --> 00:45:41.480
Ya haven't been in a 
karuta match before, have ya?

00:45:41.480 --> 00:45:43.590
<i>Ain't that why 
I'm doin' special training?!</i>

00:45:43.920 --> 00:45:47.320
When we were kids, 
weren't ya really good at playin' karuta?!

00:45:48.220 --> 00:45:49.310
Oh, now that ya mention it...

00:45:49.310 --> 00:45:53.170
In grade school, I entered some open-to-all karuta competition, didn't I?

00:45:53.170 --> 00:45:57.150
I was so surprised when, outta the blue, 
ya won the championship, Heiji!

00:45:57.150 --> 00:46:00.060
That was long ago. 
Don't remember it anymore.

00:46:00.060 --> 00:46:02.090
<i>I remember it very well.</i>

00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:04.890
Even when Mikiko asked me 
to sign up as a club member...

00:46:04.890 --> 00:46:08.410
That was the first thing 
that came to mind, too!

00:46:08.410 --> 00:46:09.520
<i>Oh?</i>

00:46:09.520 --> 00:46:13.520
<i>So, are you done reminiscing? 
I'm gonna hang up pretty soon.</i>

00:46:13.520 --> 00:46:14.830
What's with that tone of voice?!

00:46:15.560 --> 00:46:18.420
<i>Ya wanna get this call 
with me over with that quickly?</i>

00:46:18.850 --> 00:46:20.650
I ain't sayin' that, now, am I?!

00:46:20.650 --> 00:46:23.580
<i>Yeah, yeah... 
I'll be fine, even if you're not here, Heiji!</i>

00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:24.940
Huh?
What's goin' on?!

00:46:24.940 --> 00:46:26.930
Enough! 
Heiji, you big idiot!

00:46:29.120 --> 00:46:31.430
Sheesh. 
What's wrong with you, Heiji?

00:46:33.310 --> 00:46:36.040
Jeez. 
What's wrong with her?

00:46:37.160 --> 00:46:39.130
Oh, well.

00:46:41.660 --> 00:46:44.690
Hey, it's me. 
There's a small favor I'd like to ask of you.

00:46:45.050 --> 00:46:47.350
Yeah, that's it. Please do.

00:46:48.340 --> 00:46:51.070
Man, am I tired!

00:46:51.070 --> 00:46:52.410
Welcome back, sir!

00:46:52.410 --> 00:46:53.110
Thanks.

00:46:53.110 --> 00:46:57.730
I never thought we'd get caught up in a case, coming all the way to Osaka.

00:47:00.020 --> 00:47:01.520
Dad, where's Conan-kun?

00:47:01.520 --> 00:47:04.670
He said he wanted us to head 
back together, and got in the car...

00:47:04.670 --> 00:47:06.730
But now that 
we made it to the hotel...

00:47:06.730 --> 00:47:09.380
He ran off, saying he's going
to talk with Achiwa-san or something.

00:47:09.380 --> 00:47:10.760
Wha...?

00:47:10.760 --> 00:47:13.260
Oh, Conan-kun...

00:47:13.260 --> 00:47:15.310
If the person I 
thought is behind this...

00:47:15.790 --> 00:47:18.600
Then it doesn't seem like 
Achiwa-san will be targeted tonight.

00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:26.670
What is it, Ran-neechan?

00:47:26.670 --> 00:47:28.330
<i>Have you finished 
what you needed to do?</i>

00:47:28.330 --> 00:47:29.450
Oh, yeah.

00:47:29.450 --> 00:47:31.300
<i>Then hurry back 
to the room, okay?</i>

00:47:31.300 --> 00:47:33.660
<i>We had all that happen, 
so I'm just so worried!</i>

00:47:33.660 --> 00:47:35.770
Yeah, okay. 
I'll be right there!

00:47:42.230 --> 00:47:43.500
There.

00:47:43.500 --> 00:47:45.700
Now I can track him, 
even if he goes outside.

00:47:45.700 --> 00:47:46.460
Huh?

00:47:46.460 --> 00:47:48.570
Wait, isn't she...?

00:47:49.450 --> 00:47:51.720
What is she doing here?

00:47:54.990 --> 00:47:56.620
<i>"We promised each other that..."</i>

00:47:59.160 --> 00:48:01.690
Whoa! 
That's awesome, Miss!

00:48:01.690 --> 00:48:04.210
I knew it. I can't be 
your practicing partner.

00:48:04.210 --> 00:48:06.430
Come on! Don't you 
know that was dangerous?!

00:48:06.430 --> 00:48:07.530
Just a little closer and I'd be...

00:48:07.530 --> 00:48:08.260
I'm back!

00:48:08.260 --> 00:48:09.090
Oh! Conan-kun!

00:48:09.470 --> 00:48:11.700
A trustworthy 
helper came with me!

00:48:13.450 --> 00:48:14.240
Oh?

00:48:14.240 --> 00:48:14.750
Huh?

00:48:14.750 --> 00:48:15.700
Who's that?

00:48:16.140 --> 00:48:17.250
What...?

00:48:17.250 --> 00:48:19.190
Heiji's mother?!

00:48:19.190 --> 00:48:21.120
You see, I heard about 
what happened from Heiji...

00:48:21.120 --> 00:48:23.030
And rushed right over.

00:48:23.030 --> 00:48:24.480
What...? Why?

00:48:27.880 --> 00:48:30.120
To help you, Kazuha-chan.

00:48:30.120 --> 00:48:31.870
Aren't you doing 
special karuta training?

00:48:31.870 --> 00:48:33.700
Well, I am, but...

00:48:33.700 --> 00:48:35.910
I'll be your opponent.

00:48:35.910 --> 00:48:39.520
Though, as a <i>former </i>queen, 
I may be inadequate.

00:48:39.520 --> 00:48:41.060
Former queen?

00:48:41.060 --> 00:48:43.380
This was none 
other than Heiji's request.

00:48:43.380 --> 00:48:47.050
I shall teach you 
everything I know.

00:48:47.050 --> 00:48:51.510
However, due to a lack of time, 
the training will be particularly intense.

00:48:51.510 --> 00:48:53.240
Are you fine with that, regardless?

00:48:54.930 --> 00:48:57.810
Yes, I am. 
I'll do the best I can.

00:49:04.670 --> 00:49:08.230
I knew you'd come, 
Inspector Ayanokouji.

00:49:08.230 --> 00:49:10.920
It seems we are 
thinking the same thing.

00:49:10.920 --> 00:49:11.820
Yeah.

00:49:11.820 --> 00:49:14.950
Is the little detective not with you?

00:49:14.950 --> 00:49:17.180
I'm havin' him keep 
watch over Achiwa-san.

00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:20.430
I see. 
Excellent teamwork.

00:49:20.430 --> 00:49:24.190
Yes, but I'm regrettin' 
that I chose this end.

00:49:24.190 --> 00:49:28.340
Because I never thought 
she lived in such a huge house!

00:49:36.530 --> 00:49:38.990
Thank you for 
all your hard work.

00:49:39.850 --> 00:49:44.250
My name is Iori. 
I serve Momiji-ojousama.

00:49:45.120 --> 00:49:47.760
Why not take a short 
break and have some tea?

00:49:53.650 --> 00:49:56.050
So he came here, worried about me...

00:49:57.620 --> 00:50:00.210
My future husband.

00:50:08.790 --> 00:50:14.180
<i>"...incessantly bombarded by the waves, but the color of the dye does not change."</i>

00:50:14.180 --> 00:50:15.030
Oh, no!

00:50:15.030 --> 00:50:17.450
Somehow, it doesn't 
look like he's left the hotel.

00:50:18.050 --> 00:50:23.700
<i>"A bit like the waves that 
pound the shores of Sumiyoshi..."</i>

00:50:20.200 --> 00:50:22.580
You battle on 
through difficulty quite well.

00:50:22.580 --> 00:50:25.580
To tell you the truth, I did not believe you would make it this far.

00:50:25.580 --> 00:50:28.080
How about you rest a while now?

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:30.000
I... I can keep going!

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.250
Resting is also a 
splendid part of training.

00:50:34.070 --> 00:50:38.120
I shall return with some porridge.

00:50:39.060 --> 00:50:40.680
Kazuha-chan!

00:50:44.870 --> 00:50:46.120
Are you okay?!

00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:48.660
Allow her to sleep.

00:50:48.660 --> 00:50:51.460
She worked quite hard, 
without sleeping even a wink.

00:50:51.460 --> 00:50:53.400
What do you 
think of Kazuha-chan?

00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:56.030
She has much more 
talent than I initially thought.

00:50:56.030 --> 00:50:57.800
Though the best four 
will definitely be hard for her.

00:50:57.800 --> 00:51:01.140
To tell you the truth, 
lasting until the final will be difficult.

00:51:01.140 --> 00:51:01.980
That can't be!

00:51:01.980 --> 00:51:04.660
Listen to what someone's saying until they're finished speaking.

00:51:07.660 --> 00:51:11.580
I only said it would be difficult. 
Never once did I say it would be impossible.

00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:13.810
What one needs to 
have in competitive karuta...

00:51:13.810 --> 00:51:15.510
Is concentration and willpower.

00:51:16.440 --> 00:51:18.490
She has those.

00:51:18.490 --> 00:51:21.260
If her heart remains unperturbed, and her mind free from obstruction...

00:51:21.260 --> 00:51:23.760
Even she has the potential to win.

00:51:23.760 --> 00:51:25.580
<b>If I show her this...</b>

00:51:25.580 --> 00:51:30.650
<b>Kazuha-chan's heart 
will be unsettled, won't it?</b>

00:51:31.880 --> 00:51:33.770
My talk will be over quickly.

00:51:33.770 --> 00:51:35.520
Please calm down and take a seat.

00:51:35.520 --> 00:51:36.800
Honestly!

00:51:36.800 --> 00:51:38.840
It's almost the time 
we have to get moving, too.

00:51:38.840 --> 00:51:41.070
So, what business 
do you have with me?

00:51:41.070 --> 00:51:44.380
It's about Yajima-san's murder.

00:51:44.380 --> 00:51:46.440
Wasn't that done by a burglar?

00:51:46.440 --> 00:51:47.860
Was it, now?

00:51:47.860 --> 00:51:48.330
Huh?

00:51:48.970 --> 00:51:52.960
According to my reasoning, 
it was a planned murder in cold blood.

00:51:52.960 --> 00:51:54.290
That's absurd!

00:51:54.290 --> 00:51:57.030
Yajima-san certainly wasn't 
someone of good character.

00:51:57.030 --> 00:51:59.970
But was there someone who resented him enough to kill him?

00:51:59.970 --> 00:52:01.250
What about you?

00:52:01.250 --> 00:52:02.590
Nonsense!

00:52:02.590 --> 00:52:03.480
Why would I...

00:52:03.480 --> 00:52:04.770
Sekine-san.

00:52:04.770 --> 00:52:08.210
You've missed out on winning the Satsuki Cup for two consecutive years.

00:52:08.210 --> 00:52:10.980
Because you were defeated by Yajima-san in the final both times.

00:52:11.710 --> 00:52:14.710
If Yajima-san were to die, you would...

00:52:14.710 --> 00:52:16.530
Stop with the idiocy!

00:52:16.530 --> 00:52:18.590
Of course I want to 
win the championship!

00:52:18.590 --> 00:52:22.560
But wouldn't killing my rival to do so be going a little overboard?

00:52:22.560 --> 00:52:25.850
And the police say it was a burglar in the first place, so why are you saying that?

00:52:25.850 --> 00:52:27.540
There are several reasons.

00:52:28.180 --> 00:52:32.040
First, there are too many peculiarities in the way things were ransacked for this to be a robbery.

00:52:32.040 --> 00:52:36.560
In other words, how the murderer didn't lay even a finger on anything related to karuta.

00:52:37.210 --> 00:52:40.630
That ain't connected 
with killing someone, is it?

00:52:40.630 --> 00:52:42.090
I see.

00:52:42.090 --> 00:52:47.120
I'm certain that, due to the murderer remembering his attachment to karuta...

00:52:47.120 --> 00:52:50.120
Was unable to 
handle them roughly.

00:52:50.120 --> 00:52:53.840
"Detectives" sure 
think of weird things.

00:52:53.840 --> 00:52:57.550
But whatever you two 
wanna guess, it's all on you.

00:52:58.460 --> 00:53:02.030
Anyhow, this don't concern me.

00:53:00.150 --> 00:53:01.030
Crap!

00:53:02.030 --> 00:53:03.080
Oh, yeah!

00:53:03.080 --> 00:53:04.030
Huh? What?

00:53:04.030 --> 00:53:07.280
The floor of that 
detached hallway creaks.

00:53:07.600 --> 00:53:10.160
D'ya remember 
the creaking sounds?

00:53:10.160 --> 00:53:11.820
What about 'em?

00:53:11.820 --> 00:53:13.400
That sound's only there.

00:53:13.400 --> 00:53:16.670
If someone had entered from afar, he would have immediately noticed.

00:53:16.670 --> 00:53:20.000
However, there was no evidence of a struggle near the body.

00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:20.820
I get it.

00:53:20.820 --> 00:53:24.180
It sounds like ya wanna say the 
intruder was acquainted with Yajima...

00:53:24.180 --> 00:53:25.790
But that ain't right!

00:53:25.790 --> 00:53:29.410
Even in practicing, karuta requires considerable concentration.

00:53:29.410 --> 00:53:33.180
Once concentrating, ya 
don't notice even the tiniest sound.

00:53:33.180 --> 00:53:37.300
That's why Yajima didn't know someone came in, and got killed.

00:53:37.300 --> 00:53:38.940
That's not possible.

00:53:38.940 --> 00:53:42.940
Yajima's fatal wound was 
right in the center of his head.

00:53:42.940 --> 00:53:47.230
If he had continued his karuta, without noticing the intruder...

00:53:47.230 --> 00:53:49.230
His wound should be 
on the back of his head...

00:53:49.230 --> 00:53:51.830
Or on his temporal lobe.

00:53:51.830 --> 00:53:55.320
In other words, if Yajima-san and the murderer hadn't been acquainted...

00:53:55.320 --> 00:53:57.860
He would not have that wound.

00:53:57.860 --> 00:54:00.090
The killer was very 
knowledgeable about karuta...

00:54:00.090 --> 00:54:04.070
Was an acquaintance of Yajima-san, and lacks an alibi during the time the crime took place.

00:54:04.070 --> 00:54:07.620
Furthermore, they were someone who had something to gain from his death.

00:54:07.620 --> 00:54:11.710
How strange. 
Those all match me perfectly.

00:54:12.450 --> 00:54:13.140
But...

00:54:13.140 --> 00:54:16.550
Everything ya said 
now is just conjecture.

00:54:16.550 --> 00:54:19.920
If ya wanna make me out to be the killer, ya gotta have some proof.

00:54:21.320 --> 00:54:23.820
Sekine-sama, it's time. 
Please come with me.

00:54:23.820 --> 00:54:25.680
Sure, I'll be right there.

00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:28.370
Too bad. It's already time.

00:54:28.370 --> 00:54:29.070
See ya.

00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:31.830
Let me ask you 
just one more thing.

00:54:31.830 --> 00:54:33.420
Ya don't give up, do ya?!

00:54:33.420 --> 00:54:34.160
What is it?!

00:54:34.160 --> 00:54:37.070
You see, something you 
said caught my attention.

00:54:37.070 --> 00:54:39.360
I don't know if you 
remember it or not, but...

00:54:39.380 --> 00:54:42.440
If the legendary Satsuki Cup was discontinued because of Yajima's death...

00:54:42.440 --> 00:54:44.500
Wouldn't that mean 
Yajima died in vain?

00:54:44.500 --> 00:54:45.920
I mean, wasn't he beaten down?!

00:54:45.940 --> 00:54:48.180
...is what you said, 
if I remember correctly.

00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:50.820
Normally, when one hears 
that the weapon was a sword...

00:54:50.820 --> 00:54:52.930
One would wonder whether 
he was slashed or stabbed.

00:54:52.930 --> 00:54:56.680
Nevertheless, you 
said he was "beaten down".

00:54:56.680 --> 00:55:01.840
Only the murderer would know that the sword was rusted, and couldn't be removed from its sheath.

00:55:01.840 --> 00:55:04.940
So how did you know 
he was beaten to death?

00:55:04.940 --> 00:55:07.880
B-Because I saw his 
body at the crime scene.

00:55:07.880 --> 00:55:09.050
Isn't that enough?!

00:55:09.050 --> 00:55:12.700
Just before you came, 
a cover was placed over the body.

00:55:13.350 --> 00:55:16.730
You didn't have the 
chance to see his body directly.

00:55:18.730 --> 00:55:21.460
I-I just sort of figured...

00:55:21.460 --> 00:55:26.210
From seeing how the blood was splattered, 
I just sort of figured he had been beaten down!

00:55:26.210 --> 00:55:29.330
Anyway, I've got no 
connection to this murder!

00:55:29.330 --> 00:55:31.620
Man, how rude!

00:55:32.200 --> 00:55:35.620
How will he act, 
now that he's shaken up?

00:55:35.620 --> 00:55:37.480
All that's left to be cautious for...

00:55:37.480 --> 00:55:39.730
Is the match's venue, right?

00:55:39.730 --> 00:55:43.640
Yeah. I looked it up earlier, and it looks like it's gonna be pretty bothersome.

00:55:43.640 --> 00:55:46.720
This place is huge, 
all things considered!

00:55:47.740 --> 00:55:50.050
Oh? What's this building 
in the middle of the cliff?

00:55:50.050 --> 00:55:51.490
That's Satsuki Tower.

00:55:51.490 --> 00:55:52.940
"Satsuki"...?

00:55:52.940 --> 00:55:53.900
That's right.

00:55:53.900 --> 00:55:56.530
It's said that in memory 
of his wife, Satsuki-san...

00:55:56.530 --> 00:55:59.750
Achiwa-san christened it as 
such, once it was completed.

00:55:59.750 --> 00:56:00.940
I see.

00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:04.280
So it can only 
be climbed once a year...

00:56:04.280 --> 00:56:08.760
And doing so is reserved for only Achiwa-san and the two finalists, huh?

00:56:08.760 --> 00:56:10.910
As for the match particulars...

00:56:10.910 --> 00:56:13.920
There's a system that uses cameras and 
microphones installed in the venue...

00:56:13.920 --> 00:56:18.000
Which can deliver the match to a separate venue reserved for spectators across the river.

00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:19.620
That's really complicated.

00:56:20.680 --> 00:56:23.710
Through its air conditioning system, 
the inside of venue for the match...

00:56:23.710 --> 00:56:26.460
Has both its temperature and humidity 
always set to, and kept at, a constant...

00:56:26.460 --> 00:56:31.300
And the soundproof walls of the building completely shut out any outside noise.

00:56:31.300 --> 00:56:33.760
It seems it's made up of 
the latest and greatest system.

00:56:33.760 --> 00:56:38.490
In other words, it's unarguably the greatest competition venue created solely for karuta.

00:56:46.020 --> 00:56:47.280
I'm hungry...

00:56:47.280 --> 00:56:48.780
How 'bout we go to the buffet?

00:56:48.780 --> 00:56:50.510
I wanna have cake!

00:56:50.510 --> 00:56:52.960
Then, we'll be heading out.

00:56:52.960 --> 00:56:54.390
Come and enjoy yourselves.

00:56:54.450 --> 00:56:55.450
I will.

00:56:55.450 --> 00:56:56.760
Ran-oneesan!

00:56:56.760 --> 00:56:58.520
Let's hurry and go play!

00:56:58.520 --> 00:56:59.390
See you later!

00:56:59.390 --> 00:57:00.410
Later.

00:57:00.410 --> 00:57:01.630
Take care!

00:57:01.630 --> 00:57:02.790
Sorry for the wait.

00:57:02.790 --> 00:57:05.370
It's not like all the 
souvenirs will be sold out!

00:57:04.460 --> 00:57:05.370
Ma'am!

00:57:05.370 --> 00:57:05.950
Yeah, you're right.

00:57:05.370 --> 00:57:06.960
Okay, let's start training again!

00:57:05.950 --> 00:57:07.880
Where should we go first?

00:57:06.960 --> 00:57:08.780
Now, wait a minute.

00:57:07.880 --> 00:57:08.780
Let's pick through rock-paper-scissors!

00:57:08.780 --> 00:57:12.780
If you don't get a little more sleep, you won't have any stamina by the time of the actual match.

00:57:12.780 --> 00:57:14.110
I'll be fine!

00:57:14.110 --> 00:57:15.780
Kazuha! 
D-Don't tell me...

00:57:15.780 --> 00:57:19.540
You had Shizuka-san, 
the former queen, train you?!

00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:20.520
Sure did.

00:57:20.520 --> 00:57:21.850
That's incredible!

00:57:21.850 --> 00:57:23.790
With that, you might... 
You might just actually...!

00:57:23.790 --> 00:57:24.990
Okay!

00:57:24.990 --> 00:57:27.820
Let's hurry back to the 
room, and continue practicing!

00:57:27.820 --> 00:57:30.050
If you want to practice so badly...

00:57:30.050 --> 00:57:32.650
Shall I be your opponent?

00:57:32.650 --> 00:57:36.370
After all, I do not believe <i>this girl</i> can advance to the final round.

00:57:38.200 --> 00:57:39.760
<i>What did ya say...?!</i>

00:57:41.200 --> 00:57:43.270
Kazuha-chan, you go rest.

00:57:43.270 --> 00:57:44.240
Ma'am?

00:57:44.240 --> 00:57:45.770
I shall play against you.

00:57:45.770 --> 00:57:47.770
Are you dissatisfied with me?

00:57:47.770 --> 00:57:52.280
Why is Ikenami Shizuka-san, 
the former queen, helping that girl...?

00:57:52.280 --> 00:57:55.280
If not, why not
 have a fair match?

00:57:55.280 --> 00:57:57.600
Since you're saying all of that...

00:57:57.600 --> 00:57:59.780
Please do.

00:58:04.690 --> 00:58:06.230
Where are Ichiwa-san and Sekine?

00:58:06.230 --> 00:58:10.220
Apparently, they're going to Achiwa Hall, the competition venue...

00:58:10.220 --> 00:58:12.210
To hold a rehearsal for tomorrow.

00:58:12.820 --> 00:58:16.300
We probably don't need to worry, 'cause a police escort is accompanying 'em while they're moving...

00:58:16.300 --> 00:58:19.740
But the problem'll be, as we thought, after they enter Achiwa Hall.

00:58:19.740 --> 00:58:21.060
What about Momiji-san?

00:58:21.060 --> 00:58:22.290
Relax.

00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:25.520
She's in Kyoto, too, so 
everyone's heading there together.

00:58:26.540 --> 00:58:28.260
Oh, sorry. Phone.

00:58:29.630 --> 00:58:33.690
I've identified the man in the 
photo you asked me to look into.

00:58:33.690 --> 00:58:35.300
What? Really?!

00:58:35.300 --> 00:58:37.700
<i>Yes. 
The contents are a bit shocking.</i>

00:58:37.700 --> 00:58:39.950
I've emailed you the details...

00:58:38.740 --> 00:58:39.950
Message has been sent.

00:58:39.950 --> 00:58:41.100
So check them later.

00:58:41.100 --> 00:58:42.250
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:58:42.250 --> 00:58:42.700
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:44.700
Edogawa Conan
Call In Progress

00:58:43.300 --> 00:58:44.700
<i>How are things 
going with the karuta cards?</i>

00:58:44.700 --> 00:58:47.210
I just started running them 
through some analysis software.

00:58:47.210 --> 00:58:48.900
Have to hand it to the professor.

00:58:48.900 --> 00:58:52.460
It looks like it can find which card he had been holding in an hour, at the earliest.

00:58:52.460 --> 00:58:53.550
Great.

00:58:53.550 --> 00:58:56.470
Let me know as soon 
as that analysis is complete.

00:58:56.470 --> 00:58:57.210
Right.

00:58:59.740 --> 00:59:00.790
Sheesh.

00:59:03.310 --> 00:59:05.420
"Nagoro Shikao"?

00:59:06.860 --> 00:59:09.400
You've made me enjoy this for the first time in a quite a while.

00:59:09.400 --> 00:59:10.560
Thank you very much.

00:59:10.560 --> 00:59:12.580
Shall we head back now, Iori?

00:59:12.580 --> 00:59:13.440
Yes, ma'am.

00:59:13.440 --> 00:59:16.070
All things considered, 
you really have some guts.

00:59:17.020 --> 00:59:20.820
With <i>your</i> skill level, it is surprising to think that you are entering the competition.

00:59:20.820 --> 00:59:22.730
Remember this well.

00:59:22.740 --> 00:59:24.490
My name is Momiji.

00:59:24.480 --> 00:59:27.370
I'm in an entirely different league from a regular leaf, like you.

00:59:27.370 --> 00:59:28.880
A-A leaf?

00:59:28.880 --> 00:59:30.580
We already know that much!

00:59:30.580 --> 00:59:35.340
I will not hold back, even if my opponent is as much as an amateur as you.

00:59:35.340 --> 00:59:37.790
After all, I have let my guard 
down for an amateur before...

00:59:37.790 --> 00:59:40.590
And suffered an entirely 
humiliating loss because of it.

00:59:41.110 --> 00:59:44.330
Never once have I had 
a more mortifying experience!

00:59:44.330 --> 00:59:47.600
And so, I shall move ahead 
with all the strength I have!

00:59:47.600 --> 00:59:49.840
B-Bring it on!

00:59:49.840 --> 00:59:52.650
Now, let's leave 
the karuta talk at that.

00:59:52.650 --> 00:59:55.380
Is it okay for you to be here?

00:59:55.380 --> 00:59:57.880
The chairman is 
worried about you, is he not?

00:59:57.880 --> 01:00:01.410
Thanks for your concern. 
But I am quite all right.

01:00:01.410 --> 01:00:04.030
Because whatever happens, 
the great detective of the west...

01:00:04.030 --> 01:00:06.410
Hattori Heiji-kun, 
will be there with me.

01:00:06.410 --> 01:00:08.410
What d'ya mean by that?!

01:00:08.410 --> 01:00:11.320
Oh? 
Have you not heard?

01:00:11.320 --> 01:00:13.540
Heiji-kun is my bodyguard.

01:00:13.980 --> 01:00:14.920
<i>WHAT...?!</i>

01:00:14.920 --> 01:00:17.240
Even last night, he went 
without a wink of sleep...

01:00:17.240 --> 01:00:19.970
Keeping watch over 
me in front of my house.

01:00:21.400 --> 01:00:23.530
Well then, 
I had better be going.

01:00:23.530 --> 01:00:26.220
I look forward to 
the match tomorrow.

01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:31.340
My, there is more to 
Heiji than meets the eye.

01:00:31.340 --> 01:00:33.530
Hey, Kazuha. Are ya okay?

01:00:33.530 --> 01:00:34.670
<i>HEIJI!</i>

01:00:34.670 --> 01:00:37.360
I dunno what kinda 
relationship ya have with that broad...

01:00:37.360 --> 01:00:40.520
But I'm gonna crush 
her in the karuta match!

01:00:40.520 --> 01:00:43.110
Just you watch, Heiji!

01:00:44.510 --> 01:00:46.100
Yes. Well said.

01:00:48.520 --> 01:00:49.560
What's wrong, Hattori?

01:00:49.560 --> 01:00:51.870
No, I dunno what it is...

01:00:51.870 --> 01:00:54.190
But something cold 
just ran down my spine.

01:00:54.190 --> 01:00:55.630
Did you catch a 
cold or something?

01:00:55.630 --> 01:00:58.630
A cold?! This ain't 
nothing cute like that!

01:00:58.630 --> 01:01:00.820
It's something 
much more ominous.

01:01:03.280 --> 01:01:04.800
Look, here they come!

01:01:05.530 --> 01:01:06.550
Chairman Achiwa...

01:01:07.300 --> 01:01:08.800
Ooka Momiji...

01:01:08.800 --> 01:01:09.810
And Sekine.

01:01:09.810 --> 01:01:11.560
They're all going together.

01:01:32.740 --> 01:01:33.210
Don't tell me...

01:01:34.770 --> 01:01:36.210
That's Sekine's car!

01:01:41.230 --> 01:01:43.660
So what's Sekine-san's condition?

01:01:43.660 --> 01:01:45.860
Based on the contact 
we've had with the hospital...

01:01:45.860 --> 01:01:47.720
It seems he has yet 
to regain consciousness.

01:01:47.720 --> 01:01:50.720
He, apparently, has a 
50-50 chance of being saved.

01:01:50.720 --> 01:01:55.250
Ooka-kun got caught up 
in the explosion, but was she okay?

01:01:55.250 --> 01:01:57.230
She didn't seem to 
have sustained any injuries...

01:01:57.230 --> 01:02:02.490
But to be safe, we're having her examined at the hospital along with her driver, Iori-san.

01:02:02.490 --> 01:02:08.040
Can we have you explain, in further detail, the situation that led to this unfortunate event...

01:02:08.040 --> 01:02:09.120
Achiwa-san?

01:02:10.100 --> 01:02:16.790
We believe the bombing of Nichiuri TV may also have been targeted at the Satsuki Cup.

01:02:18.690 --> 01:02:20.110
Hey, mister.

01:02:20.110 --> 01:02:22.710
Who is this "Nagoro Shikao-san"?

01:02:22.710 --> 01:02:25.130
W-Where did you 
get that photo, boy?!

01:02:25.130 --> 01:02:28.640
From that discomposure, 
looks like ya got some idea.

01:02:28.640 --> 01:02:30.780
If ya know him...

01:02:30.780 --> 01:02:34.630
Then won'cha tell us 
everything, Achiwa-san?

01:02:35.820 --> 01:02:39.400
You see, there was a karuta competition 
in Kyoto, called the "Nagoro Cup".

01:02:39.400 --> 01:02:42.050
It was based around an elite few...

01:02:42.050 --> 01:02:46.650
Meaning less than 20 members, who practiced fiercely every month.

01:02:47.300 --> 01:02:50.660
Nagoro Shikao-kun was its leader.

01:02:50.660 --> 01:02:52.960
He had considerable skill...

01:02:52.960 --> 01:02:57.420
And it was even said that earning the right to challenge a master was only a matter a time.

01:02:57.420 --> 01:03:00.030
But he had a strong 
fixation on the matches...

01:03:00.030 --> 01:03:04.670
And honestly, even watching him from the side, I couldn't call his karuta elegant.

01:03:05.400 --> 01:03:06.170
Hey, come on!

01:03:06.170 --> 01:03:08.920
I was faster on that one!

01:03:08.920 --> 01:03:09.930
Hand over that card!

01:03:09.930 --> 01:03:11.910
How can ya say I touched 
the wrong card just now?!

01:03:11.910 --> 01:03:13.930
Where the heck are ya lookin'?!

01:03:13.930 --> 01:03:16.730
So five years ago, Nagoro-kun...

01:03:16.730 --> 01:03:20.440
Came to Satsuki, who acted as chairwoman 
at the time, and challenged her to a match...

01:03:20.440 --> 01:03:23.940
Giving the condition that 
she end the Cup if she lost.

01:03:23.940 --> 01:03:27.100
What was he doin'? 
Challenging the master of a training hall?

01:03:27.100 --> 01:03:31.020
But there was no need for Satsuki-san 
to agree to his match, was there?

01:03:31.020 --> 01:03:34.850
In order to ensure Satsuki 
couldn't decline his challenge...

01:03:34.850 --> 01:03:37.690
Nagoro-kun leaked 
information to the press...

01:03:37.690 --> 01:03:41.900
Saying the Satsuki Cup was afraid of the Nagoro Cup, thus avoiding the challenge.

01:03:41.900 --> 01:03:43.030
I see.

01:03:43.030 --> 01:03:46.740
In other words, he drove her into a position where she had no choice but to attempt his match.

01:03:46.740 --> 01:03:49.470
And so, how did 
the challenge turn out?

01:03:49.470 --> 01:03:52.180
The match could never be held.

01:03:52.600 --> 01:03:56.850
Nagoro-kun never showed up, even after the starting time of the match.

01:03:56.850 --> 01:03:59.700
In the end, it was 
considered a forfeited game...

01:03:59.700 --> 01:04:01.290
And Satsuki was declared the victor.

01:04:01.290 --> 01:04:05.340
As for Nagoro-kun, the uproar among the press he caused not withstanding...

01:04:05.340 --> 01:04:10.360
Forever branded as one who ran on the day of a match, 
he became a disgrace to the name of karuta competitions...

01:04:10.360 --> 01:04:13.270
And disappeared from center stage.

01:04:13.270 --> 01:04:17.370
So what's happening with Nagoro-san and the Nagoro Cup now?

01:04:17.370 --> 01:04:20.690
The Nagoro Cup was dissolved due to absence of its chairman...

01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:23.540
And the whereabouts of 
Nagoro himself remain unknown.

01:04:23.540 --> 01:04:28.880
Could these incidents have stemmed from Nagoro's resentment towards the Satsuki Cup?

01:04:28.880 --> 01:04:30.130
I do not know.

01:04:30.130 --> 01:04:34.260
However, the one who most strongly advocated for the dissolution of the Nagoro Cup at the time...

01:04:34.260 --> 01:04:36.790
Was the now-killed Yajima-kun.

01:04:37.260 --> 01:04:38.330
What was that?!

01:04:38.330 --> 01:04:39.930
As for us at the Satsuki Cup...

01:04:39.930 --> 01:04:44.320
We wanted to settle this peacefully, 
without aggravating the situation...

01:04:44.320 --> 01:04:45.760
But even that 
didn't come to pass...

01:04:45.760 --> 01:04:48.190
So what about the 
disbanded Nagoro Cup members?

01:04:48.190 --> 01:04:52.680
We allowed them to join the Satsuki Cup if they desired, of course.

01:04:52.680 --> 01:04:55.820
Although only two 
of them ended up doing so.

01:04:55.820 --> 01:04:58.120
By any chance, were those two...

01:04:58.120 --> 01:04:59.130
Indeed.

01:04:59.130 --> 01:05:01.500
Ooka-kun and Sekine-kun.

01:05:01.500 --> 01:05:04.320
The two who got 
caught up in the last bombing?

01:05:04.320 --> 01:05:05.350
Yes.

01:05:05.350 --> 01:05:11.300
Ooka-kun, in particular, grew skilled by thoroughly training in Nagoro-kun's techniques...

01:05:11.300 --> 01:05:13.990
Thus, her numerous 
specialty cards are exactly the same.

01:05:13.990 --> 01:05:18.020
Furthermore, from the six cards with poems composed in the setting of autumn leaves...

01:05:18.020 --> 01:05:19.940
Neither of them 
have failed to get one.

01:05:19.940 --> 01:05:23.300
She, most certainly, 
could be called his greatest pupil.

01:05:23.300 --> 01:05:26.800
Why do Nagoro's specialty cards include autumn leaves in their poems?

01:05:26.810 --> 01:05:30.070
I hear it is because 
Nagoro-kun's first name is "Shikao".

01:05:30.070 --> 01:05:31.360
Venison?

01:05:31.360 --> 01:05:32.340
Yes.

01:05:32.340 --> 01:05:34.570
Venison can also be 
pronounced <i>momiji</i>, correct?

01:05:34.570 --> 01:05:42.040
I bet Nagoro wasn't too amused by having the girl he favored join and be active in the Satsuki Cup.

01:05:42.040 --> 01:05:44.650
Well, yes... 
But why now, after all this time?

01:05:44.650 --> 01:05:48.960
And what's his reason for taking the time to send an advance notice of the bombing in an email?

01:05:48.960 --> 01:05:53.050
I still dunno why he kept 
quiet for the past five years...

01:05:53.050 --> 01:05:58.300
But couldn't that advance notice email be to call attention to himself and how he was back?

01:05:58.300 --> 01:06:02.400
In which case, we would need to investigate these serial incidents in terms of Nagoro Shikao...

01:06:02.400 --> 01:06:05.560
Exacting revenge 
against the Satsuki Cup.

01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:09.010
Excuse me.

01:06:09.010 --> 01:06:10.170
What is it?

01:06:10.710 --> 01:06:15.150
It seems best to form a joint investigation 
team with the Kyoto Prefectural Police.

01:06:15.150 --> 01:06:16.000
Yes.

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:17.320
What?!

01:06:17.320 --> 01:06:18.370
Superintendent!

01:06:18.370 --> 01:06:20.330
Upon inspecting 
Sekine-san's smartphone...

01:06:20.330 --> 01:06:23.850
They found a strange email 
came in just before the bombing.

01:06:23.850 --> 01:06:24.830
A strange email?!

01:06:24.830 --> 01:06:26.770
The sender is unknown...

01:06:26.770 --> 01:06:30.400
And I hear there were only some karuta cards sent as attached files.

01:06:30.400 --> 01:06:32.210
What do those karuta cards say?!

01:06:32.210 --> 01:06:33.400
Well...

01:06:33.400 --> 01:06:36.950
"Because I left in a hurry on this journey, 
I failed to even bring something to offer at the shrine."

01:06:36.950 --> 01:06:39.930
"Please accept the dazzling blanket of autumn leaves over Mt. Tamukeyama..."

01:06:39.930 --> 01:06:41.510
That's one of 
Nagoro-kun's specialty cards!

01:06:43.790 --> 01:06:45.210
What's wrong, Hei-chan?

01:06:45.210 --> 01:06:46.890
I've gotta check right now!

01:06:46.890 --> 01:06:49.170
Momiji's in danger!

01:06:51.000 --> 01:06:52.150
<i>Is this Iori-san?</i>

01:06:52.150 --> 01:06:54.210
From that voice, 
this is Hattori-sama, correct?

01:06:54.210 --> 01:06:55.100
<i>Yeah.</i>

01:06:55.100 --> 01:06:59.760
<i>Hurry 'n check whether Momiji's smartphone has an email from an unknown sender!</i>

01:06:59.760 --> 01:07:00.980
An email?

01:07:00.980 --> 01:07:03.220
What's going on, Iori?

01:07:03.220 --> 01:07:05.040
There is a call 
from Hattori-sama.

01:07:05.040 --> 01:07:06.460
From Heiji-kun?!

01:07:06.460 --> 01:07:08.060
Pass me the phone, Iori!

01:07:08.120 --> 01:07:11.040
Momiji? 
Hurry and check your email for me!

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:13.880
<i>My email? 
What is this, all of a sudden?</i>

01:07:13.880 --> 01:07:15.600
More importantly...

01:07:15.600 --> 01:07:18.630
I'm so happy 
you called, Heiji-kun!

01:07:19.410 --> 01:07:21.550
<i>Oh? 
What is this email?</i>

01:07:21.550 --> 01:07:23.250
There's only 
some attached files.

01:07:23.250 --> 01:07:24.560
<i>Are they photos of karuta cards?</i>

01:07:24.560 --> 01:07:26.910
Wow! 
How did you know?

01:07:26.910 --> 01:07:28.800
<i>What poem is it? 
Read me the cards!</i>

01:07:28.800 --> 01:07:30.480
Oh? Sure...

01:07:30.480 --> 01:07:34.010
<i>"The autumn leaves of Mt. Mimuro are scattered everywhere by the fierce gusts of wind..."</i>

01:07:34.010 --> 01:07:35.970
Momiji! 
Listen closely!

01:07:35.970 --> 01:07:38.140
Ya absolutely 
<i>must not </i>be alone tonight!

01:07:38.140 --> 01:07:39.700
Don't even go home!

01:07:39.700 --> 01:07:41.240
Come to the Osaka 
Prefectural Police Station now!

01:07:41.240 --> 01:07:42.600
Got it?!

01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:45.700
<i>I cannot listen to that, 
even as a request from you, Heiji-kun.</i>

01:07:46.330 --> 01:07:49.300
For I must prepare for 
the Satsuki Cup tomorrow.

01:07:49.300 --> 01:07:51.000
<i>Is this really the 
time to sayin' that?!</i>

01:07:51.000 --> 01:07:52.840
<i>You might be bein' targeted!</i>

01:07:52.840 --> 01:07:55.030
I'll be fine.

01:07:55.030 --> 01:07:56.920
Because you'll be 
with me, Heiji-kun.

01:07:57.420 --> 01:08:00.290
You will protect me, right?

01:08:00.290 --> 01:08:01.450
Huh?

01:08:01.450 --> 01:08:04.350
<i>I've never forgotten 
that promise we made.</i>

01:08:04.350 --> 01:08:05.290
Promise?

01:08:05.290 --> 01:08:06.620
<i>See you soon.</i>

01:08:08.710 --> 01:08:10.630
That idiot hung up on me!

01:08:10.630 --> 01:08:13.460
But it seems she 
received a karuta email, correct?

01:08:13.460 --> 01:08:14.550
Yeah.

01:08:14.550 --> 01:08:18.650
Otaki, increase the guards around Ooka Momiji immediately!

01:08:18.650 --> 01:08:19.680
Yes, sir!

01:08:21.500 --> 01:08:25.160
This means Yajima-san was the only one who didn't have karuta sent to him.

01:08:25.160 --> 01:08:30.120
Wasn't a karuta card message also left at the scene of Yajima-san's murder?

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:31.370
In other words...

01:08:31.370 --> 01:08:34.460
After the true killer, 
Nagoro, murdered Yajima-san...

01:08:34.460 --> 01:08:38.240
He left his own 
specialty cards and left the scene.

01:08:38.240 --> 01:08:42.660
But Sekine came later, 
and further hid that handiwork.

01:08:42.660 --> 01:08:44.100
I get it.

01:08:44.100 --> 01:08:48.470
Through the message left at the crime scene, Sekine was certain that Nagoro had killed him...

01:08:48.470 --> 01:08:51.050
And in order to hide 
his former master's crime...

01:08:51.050 --> 01:08:54.980
Wrecked havoc throughout the house, 
camouflaging it as the act of a robber.

01:08:54.980 --> 01:08:59.970
Are the police saying that Sekine-kun 
was at the scene of the murder first?

01:08:59.970 --> 01:09:02.490
Yes. 
There's an extremely high likelihood of that.

01:09:02.490 --> 01:09:06.700
Actually, we had a certain someone 
analyze photos of the crime scene.

01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:10.000
From the shape and direction of the bloodstains on the karuta...

01:09:09.330 --> 01:09:10.000
All right!

01:09:10.060 --> 01:09:14.360
It should have calculated how the cards were arranged at the time of his murder.

01:09:14.360 --> 01:09:15.900
Look at the TV!

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:18.700
Because the ones on the 
right were laid out on the floor...

01:09:18.700 --> 01:09:21.370
Those are the cards that 
got Yajima-san's blood on them.

01:09:21.370 --> 01:09:24.520
The ones on the 
left are clean cards...

01:09:24.520 --> 01:09:28.180
And cards that got blood on them from being mixed in with the others later on.

01:09:28.180 --> 01:09:32.940
Then, based on the bending and such of the cards with faint blood stains...

01:09:32.940 --> 01:09:36.300
The card Yajima-san 
had been holding was...

01:09:36.300 --> 01:09:37.690
Number 32!

01:09:37.690 --> 01:09:39.270
Harumichi-no-Tsuraki!

01:09:40.320 --> 01:09:43.700
"A dam on the river cutting through mountain ravines created by the wind is..."

01:09:43.700 --> 01:09:46.570
"Upon a closer look, a pile of fallen autumn leaves that cannot be swept down the stream."

01:09:46.570 --> 01:09:50.940
As we thought, there was one of Nagoro's specialty cards at Yajima-san's place too!

01:09:50.940 --> 01:09:54.210
Look at this. These are the cards that have been used in the crimes so far.

01:09:54.210 --> 01:09:55.620
Starting from the left...

01:09:55.620 --> 01:09:57.880
There's Nichiuri TV's.

01:09:57.880 --> 01:09:59.970
Yajima-san's.

01:09:59.970 --> 01:10:01.880
Sekine-san's.

01:10:01.880 --> 01:10:04.720
And Momiji-san's, 
which we just identified.

01:10:04.720 --> 01:10:08.720
These cards all share having the phrase "autumn leaves" in them.

01:10:08.720 --> 01:10:12.580
So all of them really 
were Nagoro's specialty cards?

01:10:12.580 --> 01:10:13.230
Yes.

01:10:13.230 --> 01:10:18.730
It seems that Nagoro Shikao is, 
undoubtedly, the true killer.

01:10:19.670 --> 01:10:23.900
I never thought it possible, but to think that all this was really Nagoro's doing...

01:10:23.900 --> 01:10:24.680
My worry is...

01:10:24.680 --> 01:10:28.120
The number of cards with poems composed in the setting of autumn leaves, of which he never failed to get...

01:10:28.120 --> 01:10:30.770
Come to a total of six.

01:10:30.770 --> 01:10:31.810
What do you mean?

01:10:31.810 --> 01:10:33.930
He means there are still two left.

01:10:33.930 --> 01:10:34.560
What?

01:10:34.560 --> 01:10:39.420
If Nagoro really is using  karuta cards to call attention to himself and his deeds...

01:10:39.420 --> 01:10:42.780
He ain't gonna do something half-baked like leavin' only the two remaining cards, is he?

01:10:42.780 --> 01:10:44.920
Don't tell me there are 
others besides Ooka-kun...!

01:10:44.920 --> 01:10:48.390
The problem is the targets corresponding to those two remaining cards.

01:10:48.390 --> 01:10:52.390
If we don't get the specifics soon, it'll prolly be hard to ward off Nagoro's crimes.

01:10:52.390 --> 01:10:53.370
Impressive!

01:10:53.370 --> 01:10:57.290
It seems you two can stop 
Nagoro faster than the police.

01:10:57.290 --> 01:10:58.200
Yeah.

01:10:58.200 --> 01:11:01.520
But we need 
more information to do that.

01:11:01.520 --> 01:11:04.650
So, what happened between you and Nagoro-san five years ago?

01:11:04.650 --> 01:11:06.200
W-Well...

01:11:06.200 --> 01:11:07.650
There had to have been something!

01:11:07.650 --> 01:11:09.570
We won't let 
you say there wasn't!

01:11:10.220 --> 01:11:11.310
Yes, there was.

01:11:11.310 --> 01:11:14.580
I couldn't say so before, but 
I'm sure it'll be fine with you two.

01:11:14.580 --> 01:11:17.210
Come by my hotel room later.

01:11:17.210 --> 01:11:21.070
How about I tell you, in detail, about what happened that day?

01:11:22.820 --> 01:11:24.820
Now, you guys. 
Wait here a minute.

01:11:24.820 --> 01:11:26.830
I'm going to go 
give this to Momiji-san.

01:11:26.840 --> 01:11:27.750
Okay!

01:11:27.750 --> 01:11:28.520
We'll wait!

01:11:28.520 --> 01:11:29.330
Yep!

01:11:29.340 --> 01:11:30.540
Milady.

01:11:30.540 --> 01:11:33.000
The police contacted me earlier.

01:11:33.000 --> 01:11:35.330
It was regarding wanting to 
increase the guards at home.

01:11:35.330 --> 01:11:37.160
Yes, I don't mind.

01:11:37.160 --> 01:11:38.500
Excuse me.

01:11:38.500 --> 01:11:42.110
You're Momiji-san, aren't you?
I'm Mouri, the one who contacted you earlier.

01:11:42.110 --> 01:11:44.230
Oh, so it was you?

01:11:44.230 --> 01:11:48.090
Thank you so very much for taking the 
time to come and return something to me.

01:11:48.090 --> 01:11:49.950
Oh, no. 
It was no problem.

01:11:49.950 --> 01:11:52.390
After all, isn't 
this yours, Momiji-san?

01:11:53.420 --> 01:11:54.820
Thanks a lot!

01:11:54.820 --> 01:11:57.120
This is like my lucky charm!

01:11:57.120 --> 01:12:00.190
Without this, I didn't know how tomorrow's match would go...

01:12:00.190 --> 01:12:02.130
But now, I'll be able 
to make it through, somehow.

01:12:02.130 --> 01:12:03.740
To you...

01:12:03.740 --> 01:12:07.280
I'll bet it took a lot to extend 
a helping hand to your enemy.

01:12:07.280 --> 01:12:08.620
No, not at all.

01:12:08.620 --> 01:12:12.870
I hope she doesn't practice 
so much that her fingers hurt.

01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:14.580
What beautiful nails!

01:12:14.580 --> 01:12:17.890
These nails are to 
protect my fingertips.

01:12:17.890 --> 01:12:20.410
In karuta, one's 
fingertips are their life.

01:12:20.410 --> 01:12:23.050
So, outside of practices, 
I always have them done.

01:12:23.050 --> 01:12:24.430
Is that right?

01:12:24.430 --> 01:12:27.520
Oh, and I wanted to 
know your contact info...

01:12:27.520 --> 01:12:29.720
So I looked 
inside your pass case.

01:12:29.720 --> 01:12:31.260
And then I saw the photo...

01:12:31.260 --> 01:12:34.410
Oh, do you mean this photo?

01:12:35.640 --> 01:12:37.640
Is the one pictured here...

01:12:37.640 --> 01:12:39.070
It's Heiji-kun.

01:12:39.070 --> 01:12:39.910
I thought so!

01:12:39.910 --> 01:12:45.670
This is a photo from when I lost to Heiji-kun 
in a karuta competition I entered as a child.

01:12:45.670 --> 01:12:49.570
As I cried from losing, 
Heiji-kun said to me...

01:12:52.240 --> 01:12:53.300
Stop cryin'!

01:12:53.300 --> 01:12:56.020
When we next meet as adults, 
I'll take ya as my bride.

01:12:56.020 --> 01:12:57.350
So wait for me!

01:12:57.350 --> 01:12:59.350
R-Really?!

01:12:59.350 --> 01:13:00.840
Yeah.

01:13:00.840 --> 01:13:02.590
It's a promise.

01:13:02.590 --> 01:13:04.120
What...?!

01:13:04.120 --> 01:13:05.650
<b>He actually proposed?!</b>

01:13:05.650 --> 01:13:09.150
That's why Heiji-kun 
is my future husband.

01:13:09.150 --> 01:13:12.010
B-But it's a promise 
he made as a child, so...

01:13:12.010 --> 01:13:13.780
Child or adult, 
it makes no difference!

01:13:13.780 --> 01:13:17.520
Once a man gives his word, 
he mustn't so easily break it!

01:13:17.520 --> 01:13:19.100
Am I wrong?

01:13:19.290 --> 01:13:23.750
How could I accurately deduce what's in the heart of the girl I love?

01:13:24.550 --> 01:13:25.860
No, you're right.

01:13:25.860 --> 01:13:29.550
"The rapids rush towards a plummet, and the water is spliced into two streams by a rock."

01:13:29.550 --> 01:13:32.550
"Just like those two streams will someday rejoin, 
I believe we two will meet again in the future."

01:13:33.400 --> 01:13:40.680
I believed our hearts were connected, even if we were apart.

01:13:40.680 --> 01:13:42.960
Please tell Leaf-chan this for me.

01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:44.690
Leaf-chan?!

01:13:44.690 --> 01:13:48.290
I won't let anyone 
take a card I'm after.

01:13:48.290 --> 01:13:50.070
That's what my master taught me.

01:13:51.210 --> 01:13:53.520
<b>Momiji-san...</b>

01:13:52.220 --> 01:13:53.520
Ran-chan!

01:13:53.520 --> 01:13:54.490
Ran-chan!

01:13:55.570 --> 01:13:57.140
What're ya spacin' out for?

01:13:57.140 --> 01:14:00.480
Ran-chan, ya've been kinda weird since ya got back from sightseeing in Osaka.

01:14:00.480 --> 01:14:01.260
Sorry!

01:14:01.260 --> 01:14:03.520
Anyway, how are you doing?

01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:05.650
Well...

01:14:05.650 --> 01:14:11.000
Heiji's mom gave me homework sayin', 
"You must choose a specialty card to win the match."

01:14:11.000 --> 01:14:14.260
But I can't just go, 
"This one!" and pick a card.

01:14:14.260 --> 01:14:16.400
Do you really to 
fret so much about it?

01:14:17.650 --> 01:14:20.210
Isn't the <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i> full of love songs?

01:14:20.210 --> 01:14:22.500
Don't think about 
the matches and such.

01:14:22.500 --> 01:14:25.810
I think you just need to pick 
a song you like that strikes home.

01:14:25.810 --> 01:14:28.060
Love, huh?

01:14:28.060 --> 01:14:31.440
If it was me, 
I guess I'd go with this one.

01:14:31.440 --> 01:14:33.670
"You were gone 
before I was able to see..."

01:14:33.670 --> 01:14:35.450
Oh, that's by 
Murasaki Shikibu.

01:14:35.450 --> 01:14:39.950
It's a poem sung about a friend one's managed to reunite with, but who leaves again in the blink of an eye.

01:14:39.950 --> 01:14:41.350
Yeah.

01:14:41.350 --> 01:14:43.950
Because just when I think I've finally able to see him, he goes somewhere again.

01:14:43.950 --> 01:14:47.100
Even though I have so 
much I want to tell him!

01:14:47.100 --> 01:14:48.770
You're right.

01:14:48.770 --> 01:14:51.900
In that case, I'll go with...

01:14:53.460 --> 01:14:58.500
"I promised myself that no one would know of my love for you. "

01:14:58.500 --> 01:15:01.470
"But I couldn’t hide it in my face, and people even inquire of me what has happened.

01:15:01.470 --> 01:15:04.420
A love song about love you can't hide, 
no matter how hard you try.

01:15:04.420 --> 01:15:05.980
That might be perfect 
for you, Kazuha-chan!

01:15:05.980 --> 01:15:08.460
It was obvious, 
even to Momiji-san!

01:15:08.460 --> 01:15:11.360
Come to think of it, 
I wonder why that woman's so confident.

01:15:11.360 --> 01:15:14.360
It's like she's under the 
pretense of being Heiji's fiancée.

01:15:14.360 --> 01:15:16.430
Don'cha think 
so too, Ran-chan?

01:15:16.430 --> 01:15:17.640
Y-Yeah.

01:15:18.120 --> 01:15:25.500
<b>I couldn't possibly tell her 
Heiji-kun proposed to Momiji-san as a child.</b>

01:15:18.120 --> 01:15:25.500
<b>I couldn't possibly tell her 
Heiji-kun proposed to Momiji-san as a child.</b>

01:15:25.500 --> 01:15:26.500
What?!

01:15:26.500 --> 01:15:30.000
Nagoro came to challenge Satsuki-san the day before the match?!

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:31.150
Is that true?!

01:15:31.150 --> 01:15:33.990
Yes, while I was away.

01:15:33.990 --> 01:15:39.700
That article states that Nagoro was 
afraid of his match against Satsuki and ran...

01:15:39.700 --> 01:15:42.010
But he had actually 
come the day before.

01:15:42.010 --> 01:15:43.750
But why'd he come a day early?!

01:15:43.750 --> 01:15:47.640
No idea. We won't know the reason without asking Nagoro himself...

01:15:47.640 --> 01:15:54.400
But he may have told Satsuki his goal was to defeat her using the Satsuki Cup's karuta cards.

01:15:54.400 --> 01:15:56.180
He used <i>those</i> cards?

01:15:56.180 --> 01:16:00.950
But aren't the Satsuki Cup's karuta cards usually kept in a museum?

01:16:00.950 --> 01:16:05.860
At the time, there was no fear of them being stolen, so they were kept at my home.

01:16:05.860 --> 01:16:08.960
But ya can't hold a match without someone to read the cards, can ya?

01:16:08.960 --> 01:16:11.940
You see all the cassette tapes 
that are lined up on that shelf?

01:16:11.940 --> 01:16:15.960
Long ago, those were 
used for karuta practices.

01:16:15.960 --> 01:16:18.200
So, how'd the match turn out?

01:16:18.200 --> 01:16:20.590
It ended with a 
total victory for Satsuki.

01:16:20.590 --> 01:16:23.620
It seems Nagoro 
couldn't do a thing against her.

01:16:23.620 --> 01:16:25.870
Just when I got home...

01:16:25.870 --> 01:16:30.730
I remember him leaving through the entryway with a completely pale face, as if he were fleeing.

01:16:30.730 --> 01:16:34.110
That was the last I saw of him.

01:16:34.110 --> 01:16:37.560
Why didn't ya 
tell the police that?!

01:16:37.560 --> 01:16:41.720
If I did, there's a chance it could leak to the press or the other members.

01:16:41.720 --> 01:16:46.560
And if they knew those historical karuta cards were used for a personal match...

01:16:46.560 --> 01:16:49.500
I'm certain there would be backlash and anger among the members.

01:16:49.500 --> 01:16:52.530
Well, it's not like I 
don't get your point, but...

01:16:52.530 --> 01:16:55.630
It's not that I 
don't trust the police...

01:16:55.630 --> 01:16:58.880
But it seems that Nagoro has 
the upper hand against them.

01:16:55.630 --> 01:16:58.880
Why does something in 
this photo feel out of place?

01:16:58.880 --> 01:17:01.420
That's why I can only 
trust you two with this.

01:16:58.880 --> 01:17:03.390
Is it because Achiwa-san's car is 
different from the one he has now?

01:17:01.420 --> 01:17:03.390
Make sure there are no further victims!

01:17:03.390 --> 01:17:06.390
Stop Nagoro's crimes 
as quickly as possible.

01:17:06.390 --> 01:17:08.390
Alright. 
Leave it to us!

01:17:10.580 --> 01:17:12.880
Ran-chan, 
two isn't enough.

01:17:12.880 --> 01:17:15.020
Could'ya put in 
two more of 'em for me?

01:17:15.020 --> 01:17:17.800
My brain wants sweets.

01:17:17.800 --> 01:17:18.960
O-Okay.

01:17:18.960 --> 01:17:20.650
<b>Could she hear 
that sound just now?</b>

01:17:20.710 --> 01:17:22.560
<b>This girl...</b>

01:17:22.560 --> 01:17:24.120
<b>Not good, not good.</b>

01:17:24.120 --> 01:17:27.170
<b>I can't use the 'covering hand' 
or 'cross hand' techniques well yet...</b>

01:17:27.170 --> 01:17:28.660
<b>So I can't read 
the flow of the match.</b>

01:17:28.660 --> 01:17:30.660
<b>At this rate...</b>

01:17:30.660 --> 01:17:33.770
<b>Heiji'll... 
Heiji'll be stolen by that girl!</b>

01:17:33.770 --> 01:17:35.210
What's wrong, Kazuha?

01:17:35.210 --> 01:17:36.910
Makin' such a scary face...

01:17:38.270 --> 01:17:39.400
Heiji?!

01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:40.860
Ya get in a fight with 
someone or somethin'?

01:17:40.860 --> 01:17:42.170
Shut up, ya idiot!

01:17:42.170 --> 01:17:44.740
Ain't ya that girl's bodyguard?

01:17:44.740 --> 01:17:46.240
So go back to her!

01:17:46.240 --> 01:17:47.300
What's with you?

01:17:47.300 --> 01:17:52.230
I came to change places with the tuckered-out old lady, and play against you, too.

01:17:52.230 --> 01:17:54.130
After all, I've never 
lost to ya in karuta, have I?

01:17:54.130 --> 01:17:56.620
That was back in grade school!

01:17:56.620 --> 01:17:58.400
Ya can't be 
my opponent now!

01:17:58.400 --> 01:17:59.670
Hey, Hattori-kun.

01:17:59.670 --> 01:18:04.240
Don't you remember anything from that 
karuta competition you entered in elementary school?

01:18:04.240 --> 01:18:07.490
Like a girl who you beat in 
the competition, or anything...

01:18:07.490 --> 01:18:08.510
Oh, yeah!

01:18:08.510 --> 01:18:11.620
That was it, Kazuha! 
The karuta competition back then!

01:18:11.620 --> 01:18:14.290
The open-to-all one 
that you entered and won?

01:18:14.290 --> 01:18:15.400
Yeah!

01:18:15.400 --> 01:18:18.520
Ya know how there was a girl who was really cryin' from losing the match back then?

01:18:18.520 --> 01:18:20.910
That was Ooka Momiji!

01:18:20.910 --> 01:18:22.770
Oh, that was her?!

01:18:22.770 --> 01:18:24.590
So don't you 
remember, Hattori-kun?

01:18:24.590 --> 01:18:25.620
About what?

01:18:25.620 --> 01:18:28.620
Anything you might have 
promised Momiji-san back then...?

01:18:28.620 --> 01:18:32.120
Well, I think I only said somethin' like "do your best next time"...

01:18:32.120 --> 01:18:34.020
Anyway, 
hurry back to her, Heiji!

01:18:34.020 --> 01:18:36.670
Ya've gotta 
protect her, don'cha?

01:18:36.670 --> 01:18:37.920
That's what the police're...

01:18:37.920 --> 01:18:39.260
Fine, just go!

01:18:39.260 --> 01:18:41.780
If she gets hurt, 
or worse, before the competition...

01:18:41.780 --> 01:18:44.260
We can't even have our match!

01:18:45.300 --> 01:18:47.930
Is that so? 
I'll do that, then.

01:18:47.930 --> 01:18:50.050
Mom! 
I'll leave the rest to you.

01:18:50.050 --> 01:18:51.270
Right.

01:18:52.670 --> 01:18:57.170
"I promised myself that no one would know of my love for you. "

01:18:57.870 --> 01:18:59.580
"But I couldn’t hide it in my face..."

01:18:59.580 --> 01:19:01.990
"And people even inquire 
of me what has happened."

01:19:07.450 --> 01:19:08.990
Nagoro-sensei...

01:19:09.820 --> 01:19:13.890
Please lend me your 
strength this year, as well.

01:19:19.540 --> 01:19:21.260
Watch over me....

01:19:22.090 --> 01:19:23.630
Satsuki.

01:19:31.720 --> 01:19:39.290
<i>"In Naniwa Bay, now the flowers are blossoming after lying dormant all winter."</i>

01:19:41.060 --> 01:19:49.300
<i>"Now the spring has come 
and the flowers are blossoming."</i>

01:19:51.300 --> 01:19:59.810
<i>"Now the spring has come 
and the flowers are blossoming."</i>

01:20:01.560 --> 01:20:08.950
<i>"The autumn winds blow through 
Mt. Yoshino to hail the darkness."</i>

01:20:04.770 --> 01:20:07.200
Kazuha-oneesan got it!

01:20:07.200 --> 01:20:10.320
We can immediately tell it's her since she looks different from all the other players.

01:20:10.320 --> 01:20:11.150
Yeah!

01:20:11.150 --> 01:20:13.830
If only Conan had seen her, too!

01:20:11.150 --> 01:20:13.830
<b>Isn't that her aikido uniform?</b>

01:20:13.830 --> 01:20:15.770
He couldn't help it.

01:20:15.770 --> 01:20:18.940
It seems he has somewhere 
he wants to go with Heiji-san.

01:20:18.940 --> 01:20:19.710
I know!

01:20:19.710 --> 01:20:24.270
Let's send Conan-kun the picture of Genta-kun we took at the souvenir shop before!

01:20:24.270 --> 01:20:25.700
The one where 
they were angry at him?

01:20:28.820 --> 01:20:30.620
It sounds like it's started.

01:20:30.620 --> 01:20:31.120
Indeed.

01:20:31.120 --> 01:20:35.290
Well, even Nagoro shouldn't be able to get in with all this top security.

01:20:35.290 --> 01:20:37.210
Indeed. 
And not only Nagoro...

01:20:37.210 --> 01:20:43.060
Not a single person who was not registered as staff beforehand can enter.

01:20:43.060 --> 01:20:45.470
The advance inspection 
was completely thorough, too.

01:20:45.470 --> 01:20:48.050
We will not allow 
Nagoro to do as he pleases.

01:20:48.710 --> 01:20:50.140
What's wrong, Hattori?

01:20:50.140 --> 01:20:51.550
No, it's nothing.

01:20:53.430 --> 01:20:54.680
Who's this?

01:20:54.680 --> 01:20:57.140
Oh, it's from Mitsuhiko?

01:20:57.140 --> 01:20:59.690
Man, what are
 you doing, Genta?

01:20:59.690 --> 01:21:02.070
Grabbing a hold of a 
thousand sheets together like that.

01:21:03.250 --> 01:21:05.170
So that's it!

01:21:07.190 --> 01:21:10.760
"The promise you made to me was as beautiful as the dew on the grass..."

01:21:30.110 --> 01:21:32.360
I shoulda known. 
Momiji's the first to make it out.

01:21:32.360 --> 01:21:34.150
What about Kazuha-oneesan?

01:21:34.150 --> 01:21:35.910
Not yet, it seems.

01:21:35.910 --> 01:21:37.230
Hey! 
Isn't that her?!

01:21:37.230 --> 01:21:39.550
You're right!
It's Kazuha-oneesan!

01:21:39.550 --> 01:21:40.410
All right!

01:21:40.410 --> 01:21:42.410
Way to go, Kazuha-chan!

01:21:42.480 --> 01:21:46.420
<b>Making it through the 
first round is quite a good start.</b>

01:21:52.420 --> 01:21:55.180
Oh, Sekine-san? Sekine-san!

01:22:40.180 --> 01:22:41.720
Thank you.

01:22:41.720 --> 01:22:44.730
To think that girl 
made it to the finals!

01:22:44.730 --> 01:22:47.730
It's certainly a surprise that there was still someone else with such talent!

01:22:49.750 --> 01:22:51.650
Yay!
Awesome!

01:22:51.650 --> 01:22:52.900
I wonder if she can win?

01:22:52.900 --> 01:22:54.030
Of course she can!

01:22:54.030 --> 01:22:57.530
That's Kazuha for ya! 
She'll take the cup if she keeps this up!

01:22:57.630 --> 01:22:59.760
<b>I wonder if Kazuha realizes?</b>

01:22:59.760 --> 01:23:04.450
<b>If she happens to win against Momiji-san, she has to confess her love to Hattori-kun!</b>

01:23:04.450 --> 01:23:07.550
Kazuha's sure doing her best.

01:23:07.550 --> 01:23:09.570
It's finally down to the 
deciding match with Momiji-san.

01:23:09.570 --> 01:23:10.480
Yeah.

01:23:10.650 --> 01:23:11.990
What?!

01:23:11.990 --> 01:23:14.120
Sekine-san regained conciousness?

01:23:14.120 --> 01:23:17.500
Oh, so it really 
was just as we thought.

01:23:17.500 --> 01:23:18.770
Understood.

01:23:18.770 --> 01:23:21.120
We'll leave this end to the Kyoto 
Prefectural Police and return immediately.

01:23:21.120 --> 01:23:23.150
Sekine-san's come to?

01:23:23.150 --> 01:23:23.850
Yes.

01:23:23.850 --> 01:23:26.960
It seems he did pretty 
much just as Hei-chan inferred.

01:23:26.960 --> 01:23:29.980
But why was Sekine-san 
at Yajima-san's home?

01:23:30.040 --> 01:23:34.530
It seems Yajima-san had recently been hunting around for Nagoro here.

01:23:34.530 --> 01:23:36.110
Sekine-san discovered that...

01:23:36.110 --> 01:23:39.500
And believing he may find information regarding his former master...

01:23:39.500 --> 01:23:41.570
He had apparently been 
keeping his eye on Yajima-san.

01:23:41.570 --> 01:23:44.820
Because of that, he 
realized something seemed amiss...

01:23:44.820 --> 01:23:46.350
And discovered his body?

01:23:46.350 --> 01:23:47.370
Perhaps so.

01:23:47.370 --> 01:23:52.040
I believe we'll get the details once we return to Osaka and question Sekine-san directly.

01:23:52.040 --> 01:23:53.170
Right.

01:23:53.170 --> 01:23:55.070
Then please allow the Kyoto Prefectural Police to handle this area.

01:23:55.070 --> 01:23:55.950
Yes, sir.

01:23:55.950 --> 01:23:58.410
Oh, please wait! 
I'll go with you!

01:24:02.870 --> 01:24:04.140
This is the end.

01:24:04.140 --> 01:24:09.000
But why do I need 
to plant dynamite here...?

01:24:12.500 --> 01:24:14.300
What's that smoke? 
Is there a fire?

01:24:14.300 --> 01:24:16.600
No, if that was it, the fire sprinkler system should have started up!

01:24:16.600 --> 01:24:17.560
Don't tell me it's a bomb?!

01:24:17.560 --> 01:24:19.200
Come on, don't 
even joke about that!

01:24:19.200 --> 01:24:21.750
Ain't it kinda noisy out there?

01:24:21.750 --> 01:24:24.270
What is in the woods to the west?

01:24:24.270 --> 01:24:27.350
Well, there's only an 
old storage shed in that area.

01:24:27.350 --> 01:24:29.020
What happened on 
the surveillance cameras?

01:24:29.020 --> 01:24:31.490
That area's outside of the premises, 
so there are no cameras!

01:24:31.490 --> 01:24:32.290
What?!

01:24:33.620 --> 01:24:35.190
Come on.
Don't tell me that smoke is...

01:24:35.190 --> 01:24:36.460
Yeah. Let's go!

01:24:40.800 --> 01:24:44.800
That's Satsuki Tower, 
the place we're heading to.

01:24:47.810 --> 01:24:49.840
What's this smell?

01:24:49.840 --> 01:24:53.720
Oh, that's because the 
elevator was inspected recently.

01:24:53.720 --> 01:24:56.550
It must be the smell from the lubricating oil they used at the time.

01:24:56.550 --> 01:24:57.190
Does it bother you?

01:24:57.190 --> 01:24:59.640
No, it's not that.

01:24:59.640 --> 01:25:01.260
I just might be gettin' excited.

01:25:01.260 --> 01:25:04.640
It gets your heart pounding. 
Is that how you feel?

01:25:04.640 --> 01:25:09.170
Well, I didn't think I'd 
actually make it this far...

01:25:09.170 --> 01:25:11.710
So it <i>is </i>really pounding, 
but yours ain't, right?

01:25:11.710 --> 01:25:14.610
No, it feels as though my 
heart will leap out of my mouth.

01:25:15.940 --> 01:25:21.720
I'm just so, so worried about what kind of face Heiji-kun will make when he hears my confession of love.

01:25:22.620 --> 01:25:26.160
<b>I can't lose! 
I absolutely can't lose!</b>

01:25:27.780 --> 01:25:29.720
You cannot come any closer!

01:25:29.720 --> 01:25:31.370
What happened here?

01:25:31.370 --> 01:25:31.890
Inspector!

01:25:31.890 --> 01:25:33.630
Was it bombed?

01:25:33.630 --> 01:25:35.560
Yes. 
There's one victim.

01:25:35.560 --> 01:25:37.820
Due to the body 
being severely damaged...

01:25:37.820 --> 01:25:40.590
It's not in a state where we can immediately confirm their identity.

01:25:40.590 --> 01:25:41.680
I see.

01:25:41.680 --> 01:25:45.600
So the question is when and how the bomb was planted here?

01:25:45.600 --> 01:25:49.770
Well from looking at the circumstances, 
there's a possibility that the victim brought it with him.

01:25:49.770 --> 01:25:50.600
What?!

01:25:50.600 --> 01:25:53.370
So Nagoro bombed himself by mistake?

01:25:51.400 --> 01:25:53.370
Inform the station immediately!

01:25:53.890 --> 01:25:54.640
Yes, sir!

01:25:56.990 --> 01:25:59.020
Yes? 
This is Ayanokouji.

01:26:01.620 --> 01:26:02.700
What is it, Kudo?

01:26:02.700 --> 01:26:05.260
Hattori, take a look at that.

01:26:05.260 --> 01:26:06.220
What is this?

01:26:06.220 --> 01:26:07.270
A ring?

01:26:07.270 --> 01:26:09.220
Yeah. 
Probably the victim's.

01:26:09.220 --> 01:26:11.500
What happened, you two?

01:26:11.500 --> 01:26:14.290
Look at this ring. 
It may be evidence left behind.

01:26:14.290 --> 01:26:16.130
An awfully extreme ring, is it not?

01:26:16.130 --> 01:26:18.790
Yeah. 
Nothin' less from one this huge.

01:26:18.790 --> 01:26:20.860
Wait, a large ring?

01:26:23.670 --> 01:26:24.650
Kaieda Tougo!

01:26:24.650 --> 01:26:25.520
Huh?

01:26:25.520 --> 01:26:28.410
By Kaieda, ya mean the guy who was Achiwa-san's secretary?

01:26:28.410 --> 01:26:29.130
Yeah!

01:26:29.130 --> 01:26:33.290
I'm certain this is the ring 
Kaieda-san wore on his thumb!

01:26:33.290 --> 01:26:36.040
In that case, is this 
"Kaieda" the true killer?

01:26:36.040 --> 01:26:36.800
No.

01:26:36.800 --> 01:26:42.150
If we hadn't found this ring, the body over there may have taken to be Nagoro.

01:26:42.150 --> 01:26:43.170
In other words...

01:26:43.170 --> 01:26:46.880
This explosion was camouflage intended to make it look as though Nagoro-san had died.

01:26:47.570 --> 01:26:48.670
Wait!

01:26:48.670 --> 01:26:51.540
If Nagoro was made out 
to have died at this point in time...

01:26:51.540 --> 01:26:56.570
Don't that mean the two remaining karuta cards have already been sent to someone?

01:26:56.570 --> 01:26:58.020
There are not two cards.

01:26:58.020 --> 01:27:00.590
You see, I just 
received a call from Otaki-san.

01:27:00.590 --> 01:27:05.270
It seems that, after having his secretary check Chairman Achiwa's email history again...

01:27:05.270 --> 01:27:08.280
He also received an 
email with karuta cards.

01:27:08.280 --> 01:27:11.230
That means there's only one card left?

01:27:11.230 --> 01:27:15.730
Only one card left... 
And only the final match to go...

01:27:11.230 --> 01:27:15.730
Only one card left... 
And only the final match to go...

01:27:16.200 --> 01:27:16.790
That's it!

01:27:17.650 --> 01:27:21.150
If Achiwa-san has 
already received a karuta card...

01:27:21.150 --> 01:27:22.170
That only leaves one!

01:27:22.170 --> 01:27:26.700
And the person to send that one card to hadn't been chosen yet!

01:27:26.700 --> 01:27:27.860
Don't tell me...

01:27:27.860 --> 01:27:30.990
Inspector! Look into 
Toyama Kazuha's smartphone now!

01:27:30.990 --> 01:27:32.180
What?! All right...

01:27:32.180 --> 01:27:34.040
But what is this about?

01:27:34.040 --> 01:27:37.210
Why was the one, final card left?

01:27:37.210 --> 01:27:40.940
It's 'cause they didn't know who would proceed to the final round!

01:27:42.050 --> 01:27:43.940
Which means that the target is...

01:27:44.630 --> 01:27:47.070
The three gathered in Satsuki Tower!

01:27:47.070 --> 01:27:49.200
I'm deeply sorry, you two.　

01:27:49.200 --> 01:27:50.450
Huh?!

01:27:50.450 --> 01:27:55.850
I hope the two of you exhibit the best of your abilities and show me a marvelous match.

01:27:55.850 --> 01:27:57.960
We'll do our best, sir.

01:28:01.200 --> 01:28:02.350
Ready... now!

01:28:02.350 --> 01:28:04.210
Go for it!

01:28:04.210 --> 01:28:07.340
<b>Kazuha-chan, 
show me your true strength!</b>

01:28:10.950 --> 01:28:11.840
What did you find?

01:28:12.520 --> 01:28:14.040
<i>Was there an 
email with karuta cards?</i>

01:28:14.040 --> 01:28:14.950
Yes, sir.

01:28:14.950 --> 01:28:18.230
Nagoro's specialty cards 
came in about 15 minutes ago.

01:28:18.230 --> 01:28:20.060
So it did, just as we thought.

01:28:20.470 --> 01:28:22.690
Stop the final match immediately!

01:28:22.690 --> 01:28:23.320
Understood?!

01:28:23.320 --> 01:28:24.470
This way, Kudo!

01:28:24.470 --> 01:28:25.550
Hey, where are we going?

01:28:25.550 --> 01:28:27.010
My motorcycle's faster!

01:28:27.010 --> 01:28:28.230
What?

01:28:28.230 --> 01:28:29.950
Cancel the final match?!

01:28:29.950 --> 01:28:31.500
Yes, sir! 
Understood!

01:28:31.500 --> 01:28:33.050
I'll contact the venue immediately.

01:28:38.930 --> 01:28:40.210
Oh? 
What's this?

01:28:41.200 --> 01:28:44.710
Probably an earthquake. 
And if that's all, there's no need to worry.

01:28:47.820 --> 01:28:49.700
Oh? 
I wonder what happened.

01:28:49.700 --> 01:28:51.290
Maybe it broke?

01:28:51.290 --> 01:28:52.220
What?!

01:28:52.220 --> 01:28:55.220
We had just gotten 
to the good part, too!

01:28:52.220 --> 01:28:53.320
A power outage?

01:28:53.320 --> 01:28:55.220
No, the lights are still on.

01:28:55.850 --> 01:28:57.670
Crap! 
It's already started!

01:28:57.670 --> 01:29:00.000
Yeah, so hang on tight!

01:29:04.040 --> 01:29:06.510
Hattori, how do we 
make it to Satsuki Tower?

01:29:06.510 --> 01:29:08.510
Leave that to me! 
I've got an idea!

01:29:08.510 --> 01:29:09.610
Come on, don't 
tell me you're going to...

01:29:13.050 --> 01:29:21.120
"To make a ruby red dye from the fallen leaves that cover the Tatsuta River:"

01:29:14.890 --> 01:29:18.120
<b>I knew it. 
Leaf-chan didn't even move.</b>

01:29:18.120 --> 01:29:21.120
<b>Does that mean she's 
throwing my specialty cards away?</b>

01:29:22.270 --> 01:29:23.740
"The rumors keep us from meeting..."

01:29:26.000 --> 01:29:28.880
What? 
Why is it burning so vigorously?

01:29:28.880 --> 01:29:31.450
We believe it was set 
ablaze with some sort of fuel.

01:29:31.450 --> 01:29:33.370
And the fire department 
has not come yet?

01:29:33.370 --> 01:29:37.010
The roads within the grounds are narrow, and the fire engines can't make it through!

01:29:37.510 --> 01:29:40.270
And as I recall, the 
fire sprinkler system is also down?

01:29:40.270 --> 01:29:41.520
Yes.

01:29:41.520 --> 01:29:43.330
So there's nothing more we can do?

01:30:09.000 --> 01:30:09.950
Hattori...

01:30:09.950 --> 01:30:11.880
Do you still think 
Nagoro-san's the killer?

01:30:11.880 --> 01:30:12.970
Nah.

01:30:12.970 --> 01:30:15.320
Kaieda had already 
quit the Satsuki Cup...

01:30:15.320 --> 01:30:20.040
And only <i>that man</i> coulda re-registered 
him as staff and given him the bomb!

01:30:20.620 --> 01:30:22.890
President and Chairman, 
Achiwa Kensuke!

01:30:22.890 --> 01:30:26.150
As it is, he probably intends to kill himself and take those two along with him!

01:30:26.150 --> 01:30:29.650
Like hell I'll let him do such a thing!

01:30:29.650 --> 01:30:32.900
<b>It's in the place 
that's hardest to reach.</b>

01:30:32.900 --> 01:30:34.650
<b>And Momiji-san also knows...</b>

01:30:34.650 --> 01:30:37.160
<b>That it's my speciality card!</b>

01:30:38.270 --> 01:30:40.160
<b>I bet you want to get this card.</b>

01:30:40.160 --> 01:30:42.190
<b>But I won't let ya have it!</b>

01:30:42.190 --> 01:30:44.660
<b>I win if I guard this 'til the end!</b>

01:30:44.660 --> 01:30:47.020
<b>I'm getting it! 
I'm getting it, no matter what!</b>

01:30:47.020 --> 01:30:48.860
<b>I've gotta get it!</b>

01:30:52.480 --> 01:30:54.420
<b>Shut up! 
Shut up! Shut up!</b>

01:30:54.420 --> 01:30:57.720
<b>All unnecessary noise, 
just get out of my ears!</b>

01:30:57.720 --> 01:30:58.800
What's wrong, Kazuha?

01:30:58.800 --> 01:31:00.100
Makin' such a scary face...

01:31:00.100 --> 01:31:02.770
Ya get in a fight with 
someone or somethin'?

01:31:03.560 --> 01:31:05.200
Excuse me.

01:31:05.200 --> 01:31:05.850
Oh?

01:31:07.750 --> 01:31:09.170
<b>That's right.</b>

01:31:09.170 --> 01:31:11.590
<b>I can't fight it! I mustn't!</b>

01:31:11.590 --> 01:31:13.690
<b>The sound of 
the air conditioner...</b>

01:31:13.690 --> 01:31:15.470
<b>The sound of 
my kimono rubbing...</b>

01:31:15.470 --> 01:31:16.950
<b>The sound of 
touching the cards...</b>

01:31:16.950 --> 01:31:18.600
<b>The faint breathing...</b>

01:31:18.600 --> 01:31:21.270
<b>And the beating in my chest!</b>

01:31:21.270 --> 01:31:22.930
<b>They're all my allies!</b>

01:31:22.930 --> 01:31:25.850
<b>It's fine for 'em to 
come and be within me.</b>

01:31:29.650 --> 01:31:30.860
I'm sorry about that.

01:31:31.420 --> 01:31:33.670
<b>I'll latch onto the real sound!</b>

01:31:35.400 --> 01:31:41.050
"If you tell me that you’ll wait for me, 
I’ll be sure to come back soon."

01:31:54.460 --> 01:32:00.090
To make us believe it was Nagoro-san exacting revenge against the Satsuki Cup, this entire series of incidents...

01:32:00.090 --> 01:32:02.390
Was a script Achiwa-san drew up!

01:32:02.390 --> 01:32:06.600
Five years ago, Nagoro-san had arranged to have a match against Satsuki-san...

01:32:06.600 --> 01:32:10.420
But, for some reason, he appeared the night before and had a preliminary match.

01:32:10.420 --> 01:32:14.170
Achiwa-san said it resulted in Satsuki-san being declared the victor...

01:32:14.170 --> 01:32:15.670
But there's something 
peculiar about that.

01:32:15.670 --> 01:32:18.080
The photo in the article 
we saw at the hotel, right?

01:32:18.080 --> 01:32:19.400
Yeah.

01:32:19.400 --> 01:32:21.050
The article introducing Achiwa-san...

01:32:21.050 --> 01:32:26.200
Stated that he always made his car sparkling clean the day before one of Satsuki-san's matches.

01:32:26.200 --> 01:32:27.680
But it was filthy in that photo!

01:32:27.680 --> 01:32:31.020
He didn't wash the car the day before one of her important matches...

01:32:31.020 --> 01:32:33.440
Because he knew 
Nagoro-san wouldn't come!

01:32:33.440 --> 01:32:34.320
Nothing has been 

01:32:33.440 --> 01:32:36.980
"Ever since the morning we parted, when the 
dull moon hung wanly in the sky and you seemed so cold..."

01:32:36.980 --> 01:32:39.270
I get the feeling I was quicker.

01:32:39.270 --> 01:32:42.070
Nah. 
<i>I'm</i> the one who was faster.

01:32:42.070 --> 01:32:47.580
Ain't ya the one who best 
knows which one of us was fastest?

01:32:49.080 --> 01:32:53.020
I never thought this would 
carry on to the brink of destiny...

01:32:55.820 --> 01:33:00.160
If Satsuki-san had lost in the preliminary match they had five years ago...

01:33:00.160 --> 01:33:02.010
Wouldn't that be the motive?

01:33:02.010 --> 01:33:02.870
Yeah.

01:33:02.870 --> 01:33:06.680
He silenced Nagoro-san in order to protect the honor of the Satsuki Cup!

01:33:06.680 --> 01:33:10.170
And then, upon looking at the karuta pictures left behind as evidence...

01:33:10.170 --> 01:33:13.550
Yajima-san became 
aware of Achiwa-san's crimes!

01:33:13.550 --> 01:33:16.630
But what were those 
karuta cards evidence of?

01:33:16.630 --> 01:33:21.140
What if he had inadvertently grabbed hold of a deck of karuta with Nagoro-san's blood on it?

01:33:21.140 --> 01:33:23.000
I get it! 
Fingerprints!

01:33:23.000 --> 01:33:25.680
I didn't realize this either, 
until I saw a certain photo...

01:33:25.680 --> 01:33:29.680
But those karuta probably have Achiwa-san's fingerprints on them!

01:33:29.680 --> 01:33:34.190
So that's why Yajima-san applied to have the TV station do a special feature about the Satsuki Cup...

01:33:34.190 --> 01:33:38.920
To have the Satsuki Cup's karuta cards, which would become evidence, recorded on video!

01:33:38.920 --> 01:33:39.900
Yeah.

01:33:39.900 --> 01:33:43.910
That's why the bombing at the TV station and Yajima-san's murder happened at the same time.

01:33:43.910 --> 01:33:45.350
Right.

01:33:45.350 --> 01:33:46.470
But why?

01:33:46.470 --> 01:33:51.770
Where's his reason for continuing his crimes all the way through the final here at Achiwa Hall?

01:33:51.770 --> 01:33:56.230
What if Nagoro-san's body were at Satsuki Tower, where the final's being held?

01:33:56.230 --> 01:33:59.110
That'd certainly be 
the perfect hidin' spot.

01:33:59.110 --> 01:34:03.010
So all he had planned all his 
crimes from the very beginnin'?!

01:34:03.010 --> 01:34:07.120
After all, no matter if he frames Nagoro-san as the murderer with his flawless plan...

01:34:07.120 --> 01:34:11.230
It would all be for nothing if the body were found eventually!

01:34:12.370 --> 01:34:13.400
I can see it!

01:34:13.400 --> 01:34:14.000
Yeah!

01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:20.500
"...of knowing where 
my love will take me."

01:34:21.170 --> 01:34:22.340
"You may have changed your mind..."

01:34:22.340 --> 01:34:23.040
<b>A dead card?!</b>

01:34:23.040 --> 01:34:25.200
This is bad... 
The flames are already that far up!

01:34:25.200 --> 01:34:26.340
We've gotta hurry 'n get down there...

01:34:26.340 --> 01:34:29.220
But how?
Besides, we have to put those out!

01:34:29.220 --> 01:34:31.080
There's no time to hesitate!

01:34:31.080 --> 01:34:34.370
Just think of a way 
to put out the fire!

01:34:34.370 --> 01:34:36.400
You've got to be kidding! 
Don't tell me you're going to...!

01:34:36.400 --> 01:34:38.890
Here we go, Kudo!

01:34:51.720 --> 01:34:52.540
Go!

01:34:55.140 --> 01:34:56.240
What was that?!

01:35:01.900 --> 01:35:03.950
There! 
Now keep inflating!

01:35:06.650 --> 01:35:08.680
Hurry! 
Make it in time!

01:35:08.680 --> 01:35:10.740
What? A fire?!

01:35:10.740 --> 01:35:12.330
Stay away! Get inside!

01:35:12.330 --> 01:35:14.730
Heiji! 
What're ya doin' here?!

01:35:17.920 --> 01:35:19.550
Hey! 
The direction of the waterfall changed!

01:35:19.550 --> 01:35:20.110
It's a miracle!

01:35:20.110 --> 01:35:21.370
The fire's going out!

01:35:21.370 --> 01:35:23.480
What? 
What is happening here?

01:35:27.520 --> 01:35:29.270
It looks like we 
managed to make it in time.

01:35:29.270 --> 01:35:31.770
As I expected of ya, Kudo.

01:35:31.770 --> 01:35:34.270
Heiji-kun, 
what exactly is going on?

01:35:34.270 --> 01:35:36.820
Didn't I tell ya to get 
inside 'cause it's dangerous?

01:35:36.820 --> 01:35:38.120
What? 
Conan-kun's here, too?

01:35:38.120 --> 01:35:40.950
What in the world? 
What happened, ya two?

01:35:40.950 --> 01:35:44.240
Wouldn't it be 
quicker to ask Achiwa-san?

01:35:44.240 --> 01:35:45.950
What do you mean?

01:35:45.950 --> 01:35:48.340
Get back behind me, both of ya.

01:35:48.750 --> 01:35:50.760
Why do we need ta get back?

01:35:50.760 --> 01:35:52.370
Hey, Achiwa-san.

01:35:52.370 --> 01:35:55.350
Wouldn't it be bad for you 
if we had these karuta inspected?

01:35:55.350 --> 01:35:59.000
Come on, Heiji! 
What've ya been on about this entire time?

01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:03.220
I think I'll have this old man check my answers 'bout what happened in these incidents.

01:36:03.220 --> 01:36:03.800
Huh?!

01:36:03.800 --> 01:36:09.660
It all started exactly one year ago, when Momiji won the Cup at this very place.

01:36:09.660 --> 01:36:12.680
The stack of cards 
Momiji had taken then...

01:36:12.680 --> 01:36:17.660
Very much resembled the ones her master, 
Nagoro-san, had taken in a certain match.

01:36:17.660 --> 01:36:22.820
It's true that because Nagoro-sensei trained me in offensive-style karuta, my specialty cards are the same.

01:36:22.820 --> 01:36:26.200
But it would take an 
awfully big coincidence to...

01:36:26.200 --> 01:36:28.490
Even so, that 
"coincidence" happened.

01:36:28.490 --> 01:36:32.160
There are black stains on the edges of the Satsuki Cup's karuta cards...

01:36:32.160 --> 01:36:37.850
And the late Yajima-san noticed these suddenly appeared five years ago.

01:36:37.850 --> 01:36:40.370
And what are those black stains?

01:36:40.370 --> 01:36:45.110
They're the fingerprints of the person who held them with hands that had Nagoro-san's blood spurted on them.

01:36:45.110 --> 01:36:47.340
Nagoro-sensei's blood 
spurted back on them...?

01:36:47.340 --> 01:36:50.720
Nagoro-san, who was thought to have disappeared five years ago...

01:36:50.720 --> 01:36:52.520
Was actually killed back then.

01:36:52.520 --> 01:36:53.120
What?

01:36:53.120 --> 01:36:54.390
T-That can't be!

01:36:54.390 --> 01:36:56.490
And the one whom 
those fingerprints belong to...

01:36:57.270 --> 01:36:59.520
Is the true killer 
in Nagoro-san's murder.

01:36:59.520 --> 01:37:01.950
I lose.

01:37:01.950 --> 01:37:03.630
I'll admit to everything.

01:37:03.630 --> 01:37:08.620
In return, could you refrain from using the Satsuki Cup's karuta as evidence?

01:37:08.620 --> 01:37:10.380
To the Satsuki Cup, those are...

01:37:10.380 --> 01:37:12.260
Oh, so <i>that's </i>it.

01:37:12.260 --> 01:37:15.180
There was one thing that 
I just couldn't figure out...

01:37:15.180 --> 01:37:17.180
But with that attitude, 
I finally understand.

01:37:17.180 --> 01:37:21.050
The fingerprints on these cards aren't yours, are they, Achiwa-san?

01:37:21.050 --> 01:37:23.920
No, they're mine!
They're mine, no doubt about it!

01:37:23.920 --> 01:37:24.970
It's true...

01:37:25.670 --> 01:37:29.380
That ya and Kaieda have been 
behind this recent series of incidents.

01:37:29.380 --> 01:37:34.020
But ya didn't commit the murder of Nagoro-san, which started it all, five years ago!

01:37:34.930 --> 01:37:36.620
It was Satsuki-san, wasn't it?

01:37:46.560 --> 01:37:50.340
I understood everything 
upon witnessing that sight.

01:37:50.900 --> 01:37:55.260
That Nagoro had challenged Satsuki to a match, and that she had been defeated.

01:37:58.320 --> 01:38:02.770
They used one of the cassettes I had stored as the card reader.

01:38:02.770 --> 01:38:05.770
You know what that means, correct?

01:38:05.770 --> 01:38:09.470
Satsuki had heard it countless times.

01:38:09.470 --> 01:38:12.510
Of course, it was just 
one pattern out of many...

01:38:12.510 --> 01:38:16.810
But Satsuki had memorized the order of the cards being read to some extent.

01:38:17.930 --> 01:38:21.020
She was in an overwhelmingly 
advantageous position!

01:38:21.020 --> 01:38:23.540
Nevertheless, 
Satsuki had been defeated.

01:38:23.540 --> 01:38:27.670
Nagoro's skills had far 
surpassed our expectations.

01:38:27.670 --> 01:38:31.170
I can only guess how 
scared Satsuki must have felt...

01:38:31.170 --> 01:38:36.180
For she was certain to suffer a humiliating and crushing defeat in the match the following day.

01:38:36.180 --> 01:38:40.460
It was that fear that drove 
her into committing the crime.

01:38:40.950 --> 01:38:44.630
After that, Satsuki 
lost all human emotion.

01:38:44.630 --> 01:38:48.790
She even gradually distanced herself from managing the Satsuki Cup.

01:38:48.790 --> 01:38:52.690
And then, two years later, 
she passed away due to illness.

01:38:53.340 --> 01:38:55.220
That is the truth.

01:38:55.220 --> 01:38:57.160
Please understand.

01:38:58.200 --> 01:38:59.170
Don't!

01:38:59.170 --> 01:39:00.150
Stop!

01:39:00.150 --> 01:39:02.120
Everything is Nagoro's fault.

01:39:02.120 --> 01:39:06.060
If that man had not humiliated Satsuki, none of this would have...

01:39:06.060 --> 01:39:08.060
He didn't want to humiliate her!

01:39:08.650 --> 01:39:11.800
I believe Nagoro-sensei 
went there the day before!

01:39:11.800 --> 01:39:12.650
What?

01:39:12.650 --> 01:39:14.920
Long ago, I had 
asked Nagoro-sensei...

01:39:14.920 --> 01:39:19.430
"Why do you bear such a 
grudge against the Satsuki Cup?"

01:39:19.430 --> 01:39:21.420
A grudge, huh?

01:39:21.420 --> 01:39:24.430
So it really does seem that way, when you look at it from the sidelines?

01:39:25.000 --> 01:39:28.190
However, if I don't do this, 
I can't have a match against her.

01:39:28.190 --> 01:39:32.440
I only want to win and be complimented with "you're incredible"...

01:39:34.000 --> 01:39:36.990
By my first love.

01:39:37.360 --> 01:39:38.780
F-First love?!

01:39:38.780 --> 01:39:40.060
That's right.

01:39:40.060 --> 01:39:44.540
Apparently, Nagoro-sensei started playing karuta because he was attracted to Satsuki-san.

01:39:44.540 --> 01:39:50.040
But his doctor told him he could only play karuta for a year due to an eye disease.

01:39:50.040 --> 01:39:54.050
I feel that's why he 
played karuta so fiercely.

01:39:54.050 --> 01:39:57.050
Because my master didn't have time.

01:39:57.050 --> 01:40:00.140
So he wanted to show her his true strength in a match the day before...

01:40:00.140 --> 01:40:03.060
Then hand the victory to Satsuki-san in front of everyone else?

01:40:03.120 --> 01:40:08.320
To provide justification for having his pupils, myself included...

01:40:08.320 --> 01:40:11.810
Of whom he would no longer be able to look after, to be merged into the Satsuki Cup!

01:40:11.810 --> 01:40:17.090
In other words, Satsuki-san killed Nagoro-san, not knowing that.

01:40:17.090 --> 01:40:19.380
T-That can't be!

01:40:24.650 --> 01:40:26.850
What have I done...?!

01:40:36.020 --> 01:40:37.170
W-What?!

01:40:37.920 --> 01:40:38.720
Kazuha!

01:40:42.570 --> 01:40:43.470
Kazuha!

01:40:44.240 --> 01:40:45.390
Are ya okay?!

01:40:45.390 --> 01:40:48.000
Yeah, but it's hard to stand!

01:40:53.080 --> 01:40:55.420
You guys! 
Hurry and get on the elevator!

01:40:55.420 --> 01:40:56.920
Momiji! 
Hurry 'n go!

01:40:56.920 --> 01:40:57.680
O-Okay...

01:40:57.680 --> 01:40:59.340
Hurry 'n get up! 
Let's get goin'!

01:40:59.340 --> 01:41:01.750
Forget me. 
Leave me behind.

01:41:01.760 --> 01:41:03.200
Don't be absurd!

01:41:03.200 --> 01:41:05.160
I still ain't gonna let ya die!

01:41:05.760 --> 01:41:06.830
Momiji-san!

01:41:06.830 --> 01:41:08.120
Hurry and get on!

01:41:10.770 --> 01:41:11.830
Kazuha!

01:41:11.830 --> 01:41:13.620
Climb up here!

01:41:13.620 --> 01:41:14.310
Okay!

01:41:14.310 --> 01:41:15.290
Hurry!

01:41:16.320 --> 01:41:18.690
Damn, just a 'lil farther!

01:41:19.780 --> 01:41:20.780
Gotcha!

01:41:22.950 --> 01:41:23.660
What the...?!

01:41:29.790 --> 01:41:32.670
Please, don't fall yet!

01:41:39.300 --> 01:41:40.670
Damn it!

01:41:48.200 --> 01:41:49.050
What?!

01:41:51.660 --> 01:41:53.190
Like I'll ever let you!

01:42:07.160 --> 01:42:09.080
Are you okay?! 
We're coming right now!

01:42:09.080 --> 01:42:09.600
Hey!

01:42:09.600 --> 01:42:11.040
That was close...

01:42:11.600 --> 01:42:12.100
Hattori!

01:42:17.380 --> 01:42:18.820
This is bad! 
It's collapsing!

01:42:18.820 --> 01:42:19.230
Pull back!

01:42:25.550 --> 01:42:26.240
Huh?

01:42:26.240 --> 01:42:28.530
Hey, why are they...?!

01:42:28.530 --> 01:42:30.940
Wait, don't go!

01:42:30.940 --> 01:42:32.170
Heiji!

01:42:32.170 --> 01:42:33.040
Get on, Kazuha!

01:42:34.890 --> 01:42:37.130
Hattori... 
Kazuha-chan...

01:42:37.130 --> 01:42:40.000
Please! 
Make it out of there, somehow!

01:42:45.740 --> 01:42:47.470
Heiji, is that a...?

01:42:47.470 --> 01:42:48.290
Yeah!

01:42:49.120 --> 01:42:50.580
What's wrong, Heiji?

01:42:50.580 --> 01:42:52.390
Hang on tight!

01:42:52.390 --> 01:42:56.200
Don't tell me ya plan on jumpin' all the way to that wall over there?!

01:42:56.200 --> 01:42:57.900
Ya really got it!
That's it, exactly!

01:42:57.900 --> 01:42:59.520
Ya've gotta be kiddin' me!

01:42:59.520 --> 01:43:02.280
What in the world're ya thinkin'?!
It's <i>super </i>far away!

01:43:02.700 --> 01:43:04.130
Come on, Heiji!

01:43:04.130 --> 01:43:06.700
Ain't it better to just 
jump down into the pond?

01:43:06.700 --> 01:43:07.520
Not possible.

01:43:07.520 --> 01:43:08.720
If we jumped 
down from this height...

01:43:08.720 --> 01:43:11.160
Even the surface of the water 
would be as hard as concrete!

01:43:12.470 --> 01:43:14.500
Hold on tight, Kazuha!

01:43:14.500 --> 01:43:15.660
If ya let go...

01:43:16.600 --> 01:43:17.770
I'll kill ya!

01:43:19.110 --> 01:43:19.780
Okay!

01:43:24.740 --> 01:43:26.240
We ain't gonna...

01:43:27.990 --> 01:43:31.470
Die in a place like this!

01:43:33.990 --> 01:43:35.000
What's that?!

01:43:35.000 --> 01:43:36.250
Hattori!

01:43:36.250 --> 01:43:40.400
There's still somethin' I gotta tell ya!

01:43:42.880 --> 01:43:44.990
That motorcycle...

01:43:47.170 --> 01:43:50.600
Make it!

01:44:01.150 --> 01:44:02.250
Heiji!

01:44:02.940 --> 01:44:04.360
Kazuha!

01:44:16.330 --> 01:44:18.800
Are ya okay, Kazuha?

01:44:19.620 --> 01:44:20.720
Yeah.

01:44:21.790 --> 01:44:25.230
I'm startin' to get sick 
of these dramatic escapes.

01:44:27.600 --> 01:44:28.240
Are they safe?

01:44:28.240 --> 01:44:30.820
Man, those two...

01:44:30.820 --> 01:44:33.190
I didn't know what 
would happen for a minute.

01:44:33.190 --> 01:44:34.450
By the way, Heiji...

01:44:34.450 --> 01:44:35.150
Yeah?

01:44:35.150 --> 01:44:37.980
What's the thing 
ya've gotta tell me?

01:44:37.980 --> 01:44:39.780
Huh? 
What're ya talkin' about?

01:44:39.780 --> 01:44:41.490
Ain't that what ya just said?!

01:44:41.490 --> 01:44:43.820
That ya wouldn't die 
until ya told me somethin'?

01:44:43.820 --> 01:44:45.150
Sure ya didn't mishear?

01:44:45.150 --> 01:44:46.020
No!

01:44:46.020 --> 01:44:49.220
My ears were trained <i>super </i>well during my special karuta training!

01:44:49.220 --> 01:44:51.340
If ya got a complaint, 
just go ahead 'n say it!

01:44:51.340 --> 01:44:51.900
What is it?!

01:44:51.900 --> 01:44:52.420
N-No, wait...

01:44:53.070 --> 01:44:54.270
What is it?

01:44:54.270 --> 01:44:56.400
What's this thing 
ya've gotta tell me?

01:44:56.400 --> 01:44:57.520
The thing I wanna tell ya...

01:44:57.520 --> 01:44:59.420
What is it...?!

01:45:08.400 --> 01:45:12.700
I picture you overlapping me, the two of us cuddled together...

01:45:13.660 --> 01:45:17.700
And my thoughts race along the colorless wind.

01:45:18.540 --> 01:45:22.900
Even now, I feel the warmth from when I touched your hand...

01:45:23.250 --> 01:45:28.000
Stop, please make time stop.

01:45:28.510 --> 01:45:32.700
Yes, no matter the day...

01:45:33.340 --> 01:45:38.140
I will never forget your words.

01:45:38.470 --> 01:45:40.810
I can't meet you when I want to.

01:45:41.140 --> 01:45:43.490
I can't meet you when I want to.

01:45:43.690 --> 01:45:49.780
It's so heartrending and frustrating.

01:45:50.320 --> 01:45:56.240
On the Togetsu Bridge, dyed crimson red...

01:45:56.740 --> 01:45:59.870
I wish for a day of guidance...

01:46:00.200 --> 01:46:06.500
And let my prayers be carried by the flow of the river.

01:46:12.090 --> 01:46:16.890
My heart is always besides you.

01:46:27.520 --> 01:46:31.900
Remaining unchanged, that scenery of old...

01:46:32.650 --> 01:46:36.950
Is now reflected in these eyes...

01:46:37.910 --> 01:46:42.000
Coloring beyond the season.

01:46:42.700 --> 01:46:47.170
Stock; do you still remember?

01:46:47.750 --> 01:46:52.050
Hey, when can we...

01:46:52.460 --> 01:46:57.340
See each other again?

01:46:57.640 --> 01:46:59.970
I can't meet you when I want to.

01:47:00.220 --> 01:47:02.430
I can't meet you when I want to.

01:47:02.720 --> 01:47:08.940
It's burning my heart up.

01:47:09.560 --> 01:47:15.610
When the waters are gleaming in crimson red...

01:47:15.900 --> 01:47:19.030
My thoughts with you will be connected...

01:47:19.320 --> 01:47:25.870
And my prayers will be carried by the flow of the river.

01:47:31.290 --> 01:47:36.030
I'm always looking for you.

01:47:36.970 --> 01:47:41.010
As long as I am with you...

01:47:41.430 --> 01:47:45.730
Even my anxieties will disappear.

01:47:46.100 --> 01:47:51.060
I wonder when I can...

01:47:51.650 --> 01:47:56.740
Receive your gentle embrace?

01:47:57.990 --> 01:48:04.080
Even the crimson red autumn leaves...

01:48:04.410 --> 01:48:07.540
Are announcing my ardent affection...

01:48:07.910 --> 01:48:14.210
And singing while swaying gently.

01:48:19.840 --> 01:48:24.350
I'm always, always thinking about you.

01:48:24.810 --> 01:48:29.770
I'm always, always thinking about you.

01:48:43.100 --> 01:48:45.240
Thanks for coming to see us off.

01:48:45.240 --> 01:48:47.750
We're the ones 
who need to thank ya!

01:48:47.750 --> 01:48:50.500
Come to think of it, 
what about your karuta club?

01:48:50.500 --> 01:48:51.780
About that...

01:48:51.780 --> 01:48:54.990
The school acknowledged 
that I made it to the finals...

01:48:54.990 --> 01:48:57.260
So it looks like it was 
settled without gettin' disbanded.

01:48:57.260 --> 01:49:00.380
Though I ended up 
losin' at the very end.

01:49:02.950 --> 01:49:04.500
Kazuha-chan...

01:49:04.500 --> 01:49:05.390
Come here a sec!

01:49:05.390 --> 01:49:06.500
Oh?

01:49:06.500 --> 01:49:07.580
I wonder what happened?

01:49:07.580 --> 01:49:10.640
What're they doing? 
Telling secrets?

01:49:10.640 --> 01:49:12.020
Really?

01:49:12.020 --> 01:49:13.150
Yup!

01:49:13.150 --> 01:49:15.170
Because I got the 
"though I try to hide it" card!

01:49:15.170 --> 01:49:18.150
I knew you made that 
poem one of your specialty cards!

01:49:18.150 --> 01:49:20.750
No, no...
Not just the poem.

01:49:20.750 --> 01:49:23.110
It's the name of 
the person who wrote it!

01:49:23.110 --> 01:49:24.660
Taira-no-Kanemori!

01:49:24.660 --> 01:49:26.470
In the <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i>...

01:49:26.450 --> 01:49:29.660
He's the only one with Heiji's 
"Hei" character in his name!

01:49:29.660 --> 01:49:32.440
Oh, I couldn't see 
any card but Heiji's!

01:49:33.540 --> 01:49:37.170
Afterwards, I sent Heiji a picture of the "though I try to hide it" card!

01:49:37.170 --> 01:49:39.620
Saying "this is how I feel".

01:49:39.620 --> 01:49:43.430
You sent the "though I try to hide it" card to convey your feelings...

01:49:44.050 --> 01:49:45.930
Isn't that against the rules?

01:49:45.930 --> 01:49:47.210
Momiji-san!

01:49:47.210 --> 01:49:49.180
Could ya hear us just now?!

01:49:49.180 --> 01:49:52.170
You aren't the only 
one with good ears.

01:49:52.170 --> 01:49:53.560
Oh, if it isn't Momiji.

01:49:53.560 --> 01:49:55.840
What're ya doin' here?

01:49:55.840 --> 01:49:58.820
I came to give you 
my confession, just as I promised.

01:49:58.820 --> 01:50:02.820
Though Heiji-kun's 
already confessed to me.

01:50:02.820 --> 01:50:05.010
Huh? 
What're ya on about?

01:50:05.010 --> 01:50:07.830
Here's the photographic evidence.

01:50:07.830 --> 01:50:09.290
They're making a pinky promise.

01:50:09.290 --> 01:50:11.330
So they made a 
promise to each other?

01:50:11.330 --> 01:50:14.580
And if they break that promise, 
they have to swallow a thousand needles!

01:50:14.580 --> 01:50:17.540
Waitta minute! 
What promise did we make?

01:50:17.540 --> 01:50:20.550
"When we next meet, 
I'll take ya as my bride. So wait for me!"

01:50:20.550 --> 01:50:21.800
What?!

01:50:21.860 --> 01:50:25.680
Surprisingly, this guy always has someone remember his embarassing moments.

01:50:25.740 --> 01:50:30.180
Or do you want to make it like this story from long ago never happened?

01:50:31.080 --> 01:50:33.070
Oh, I remember now!

01:50:33.070 --> 01:50:34.670
This is what I said back then!

01:50:34.690 --> 01:50:38.190
"Stop cryin'! 
Can't we just play another match sometime?"

01:50:38.190 --> 01:50:40.910
"But when we next meet, 
I'll be much stronger."

01:50:40.910 --> 01:50:42.740
"So hone yer skills 'n wait for me!"

01:50:43.190 --> 01:50:43.650
"I'll..."

01:50:44.150 --> 01:50:45.150
"...be much..."

01:50:45.740 --> 01:50:46.990
"...stronger"?!

01:50:46.990 --> 01:50:48.850
I was goin' 
against a girl 'n all...

01:50:48.850 --> 01:50:50.520
And figured I 
shouldn't hurt her...

01:50:50.520 --> 01:50:52.750
So I went easy on her and 
took the cards really gently.

01:50:52.750 --> 01:50:53.750
Iori?

01:50:54.180 --> 01:50:55.400
We're leaving!

01:50:55.400 --> 01:50:56.750
<i>Yes, Milady.</i>

01:50:56.750 --> 01:51:00.400
So long. 
I'll let you go for today.

01:51:00.400 --> 01:51:03.760
But I never let someone 
let someone take a card I'm after.

01:51:03.760 --> 01:51:06.510
Remember that well...

01:51:07.570 --> 01:51:09.290
Kazuha-chan.

01:51:11.820 --> 01:51:12.390
What?

01:51:12.390 --> 01:51:15.090
She wants to play 
karuta against Kazuha again?

01:51:21.870 --> 01:51:23.150
Sorry, were you sleeping?

01:51:23.150 --> 01:51:26.150
Didn't you know a lot 
about the <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i>, Sonoko?

01:51:26.150 --> 01:51:28.910
Yeah, because I play it 
with the family on New Year's.

01:51:29.320 --> 01:51:32.410
When I sent Shinichi a photo of the 
"you were gone before I was able to see" card...

01:51:32.410 --> 01:51:35.520
He replied back with the 
"rapids rush towards a plummet" poem...

01:51:35.520 --> 01:51:38.670
But I forgot what that means...

01:51:38.670 --> 01:51:41.700
<b>"Even if I'm now 
separated from the one I love..."</b>

01:51:41.570 --> 01:51:43.600
<i>Um, hello?</i>

01:51:41.700 --> 01:51:43.570
<b>"We'll definitely 
meet again someday."</b>

01:51:43.570 --> 01:51:46.670
<b>The poem written by Sutoku-in 
with that lovey-dovey meaning?</b>

01:51:43.600 --> 01:51:45.700
<i>Hey! Hello, Sonoko?</i>

01:51:45.700 --> 01:51:46.670
<i>Sonoko?</i>

01:51:46.670 --> 01:51:48.160
<i>Thanks for the treat!</i>

01:51:48.160 --> 01:51:49.930
Hey, wait! Sonoko!

01:51:50.890 --> 01:51:54.470
How could you have forgotten?
